0
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
BLACK SCREEN

1
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:15,330
I can't let you out, Hedwig.

2
00:01:15,340 --> 00:01:18,570
I'm not allowed to use magic outside of school.

3
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:22,970
-Besides, if Uncle Vernon...  -Harry Potter!

4
00:01:25,110 --> 00:01:26,610
Now you've done it.

5
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:33,550
He's in there. Vernon?

6
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:37,750
I'm warning you,

7
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:40,860
if you can't control that bloody bird, it'll have to go.

8
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:42,350
But she's bored.

9
00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:44,790
If I could only let her out

10
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,190
for an hour or two.

11
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:50,030
So you can send secret messages to your freaky little friends?

12
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:51,530
No, sir.

13
00:01:51,540 --> 00:01:55,430
But I haven't had any messages from any of my friends.

14
00:01:56,510 --> 00:02:00,140
Not one...all summer.

15
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:02,710
Who would want to be friends with you?

16
00:02:05,820 --> 00:02:08,280
I should think you'd be a little more grateful.

17
00:02:08,290 --> 00:02:10,010
We've raised you since you were a baby,

18
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:11,880
given you the food off our table...

19
00:02:11,890 --> 00:02:14,150
...even let you have Dudley's second bedroom...

20
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:17,190
...purely out of the goodness of our hearts.

21
00:02:17,230 --> 00:02:20,020
Not now. It's for when the Masons arrive.

22
00:02:20,030 --> 00:02:22,030
Which should be any minute.

23
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:26,630
Now, let's go over our schedule once again, shall we?

24
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:28,800
Petunia, when the Masons arrive, you will be...?

25
00:02:28,810 --> 00:02:30,000
In the lounge,

26
00:02:30,010 --> 00:02:32,540
waiting to welcome them graciously to our home.

27
00:02:32,550 --> 00:02:33,400
Good.

28
00:02:33,410 --> 00:02:34,810
And, Dudley, you will be...?

29
00:02:34,820 --> 00:02:36,810
I'll be waiting to open the door.

30
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:38,480
Excellent.

31
00:02:43,290 --> 00:02:45,290
And you?

32
00:02:45,690 --> 00:02:47,290
I'll be in my bedroom,

33
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:50,360
making no noise and pretending that I don't exist.

34
00:02:50,370 --> 00:02:52,090
Too right, you will.

35
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:53,730
With any luck,

36
00:02:53,740 --> 00:02:55,690
this could be the day I make the biggest deal of my career...

37
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:59,500
...and you will not mess it up.

38
00:03:10,450 --> 00:03:12,580
Harry Potter,

39
00:03:12,590 --> 00:03:15,450
such an honor it is.

40
00:03:18,260 --> 00:03:19,150
Who are you?

41
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:20,490
Dobby, sir.

42
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:23,260
Dobby the house-elf.

43
00:03:23,530 --> 00:03:25,220
Not to be rude or anything...

44
00:03:25,230 --> 00:03:28,830
...but this isn't a great time for me to have a house-elf in my bedroom.

45
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:32,060
Yes, sir. Dobby understands.

46
00:03:32,070 --> 00:03:35,290
It's just that Dobby has come to tell you.

47
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:37,600
It is difficult, sir.

48
00:03:37,850 --> 00:03:40,310
Dobby wonders where to begin.

49
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:42,410
Why don't you sit down?

50
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:43,580
Sit down?

51
00:03:43,590 --> 00:03:46,220
Sit down?

52
00:03:49,490 --> 00:03:51,620
Dobby, I'm sorry.

53
00:03:51,630 --> 00:03:54,150
I didn't mean to offend you or anything.

54
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:56,360
Offend Dobby?

55
00:03:56,460 --> 00:03:58,990
Dobby has heard of your greatness, sir...

56
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:03,290
...but never has he been asked to sit down by a wizard,

57
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:05,630
like an equal.

58
00:04:05,810 --> 00:04:08,530
You can't have met many decent wizards then.

59
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:11,000
No, I haven't.

60
00:04:11,210 --> 00:04:13,500
That was an awful thing to say.

61
00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:16,140
-Bad Dobby! Bad Dobby!  -Stop, Dobby. Dobby, shush.

62
00:04:16,150 --> 00:04:18,410
-Bad Dobby  -Dobby, please,

63
00:04:18,420 --> 00:04:19,950
stop.

64
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:27,190
Don't mind that. It's just the cat.

65
00:04:28,630 --> 00:04:30,090
-Bad Dobby.  -Stop!

66
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:32,800
Stop, Dobby. Please, be quiet.

67
00:04:33,430 --> 00:04:34,830
Are you all right?

68
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:39,300
Dobby had to punish himself, sir.

69
00:04:39,310 --> 00:04:42,770
Dobby almost spoke ill of his family, sir.

70
00:04:42,780 --> 00:04:44,000
Your family?

71
00:04:44,010 --> 00:04:46,800
The wizard family Dobby serves, sir.

72
00:04:46,810 --> 00:04:50,110
Dobby is bound to serve one family forever.

73
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:53,480
If they ever knew Dobby was here....

74
00:04:54,190 --> 00:04:55,950
But Dobby had to come.

75
00:04:55,960 --> 00:04:58,780
Dobby has to protect Harry Potter.

76
00:04:58,790 --> 00:05:00,450
To warn him.

77
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:01,560
Harry Potter

78
00:05:01,570 --> 00:05:07,170
must not go back to Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry this year.

79
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:09,030
There is a plot,

80
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:12,860
a plot to make most terrible things happen.

81
00:05:12,870 --> 00:05:14,500
What terrible things?

82
00:05:14,510 --> 00:05:15,530
Who's plotting them?

83
00:05:15,540 --> 00:05:19,540
Can't say.

84
00:05:19,550 --> 00:05:23,170
Okay, I understand. You can't say.

85
00:05:23,180 --> 00:05:25,320
Don't make me talk. I...

86
00:05:27,190 --> 00:05:28,310
Dobby.

87
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:30,680
Dobby, put the lamp down.

88
00:05:30,690 --> 00:05:34,290
So when they arrive at the ninth hole...

89
00:05:37,130 --> 00:05:39,020
Give me the lamp.

90
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:43,270
Dobby, stop!

91
00:05:46,370 --> 00:05:48,230
Get in there and keep quiet.

92
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:49,230
Let me go.

93
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:52,170
What the devil are you doing up here?

94
00:05:52,180 --> 00:05:53,770
I was just...

95
00:05:53,780 --> 00:05:56,840
You just ruined the punch line of my Japanese golfer joke.

96
00:05:56,850 --> 00:05:58,240
Sorry.

97
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:01,250
One more sound

98
00:06:01,260 --> 00:06:04,080
and you'll wish you'd never been born, boy.

99
00:06:04,090 --> 00:06:06,350
And fix that door.

100
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:07,890
Yes, sir.

101
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:11,920
See why I've got to go back?

102
00:06:11,930 --> 00:06:13,290
I don't belong here.

103
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:14,630
I belong in your world,

104
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:15,860
at Hogwarts.

105
00:06:15,870 --> 00:06:18,100
It's the only place I've got friends.

106
00:06:18,110 --> 00:06:20,700
Friends who don't write to Harry Potter?

107
00:06:20,710 --> 00:06:23,740
Well, I expect they've been....

108
00:06:23,750 --> 00:06:24,700
Hang on.

109
00:06:24,710 --> 00:06:27,810
How do you know my friends haven't been writing to me?

110
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:31,580
Harry Potter mustn't be angry with Dobby.

111
00:06:31,590 --> 00:06:33,310
Dobby hoped...

112
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:36,410
if Harry Potter thought his friends had forgotten him...

113
00:06:36,420 --> 00:06:40,460
...Harry Potter might not want to go back to school, sir.

114
00:06:40,730 --> 00:06:42,720
Give me those.

115
00:06:42,730 --> 00:06:43,890
Now.

116
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:45,320
No

117
00:06:58,110 --> 00:07:00,710
Dobby, get back here.

118
00:07:04,550 --> 00:07:06,080
Dobby,

119
00:07:06,490 --> 00:07:08,080
please, no.

120
00:07:08,090 --> 00:07:09,780
Harry Potter must say

121
00:07:09,790 --> 00:07:12,380
he's not going back to school.

122
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:15,550
I can't. Hogwarts is my home.

123
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:18,420
Then Dobby must do it, sir,

124
00:07:18,430 --> 00:07:21,260
for Harry Potter's own good.

125
00:07:26,140 --> 00:07:28,430
One plumber said, "Look at all that water."

126
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:32,010
The second plumber said, "Yes, and that's just the top of it."

127
00:07:43,460 --> 00:07:45,150
I'm so sorry.

128
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:47,790
It's my nephew. He's very disturbed.

129
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:49,720
Meeting strangers upsets him.

130
00:07:49,730 --> 00:07:51,960
That's why I kept him upstairs.

131
00:08:03,810 --> 00:08:06,370
You're never going back to that school.

132
00:08:06,380 --> 00:08:09,370
You're never going to see those freaky friends of yours again.

133
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:10,740
Never!

134
00:08:57,830 --> 00:08:59,330
Hiya, Harry.

135
00:08:59,970 --> 00:09:03,290
Ron. Fred. George.

136
00:09:03,300 --> 00:09:04,560
What are you all doing here?

137
00:09:04,570 --> 00:09:06,560
Rescuing you, of course.

138
00:09:06,570 --> 00:09:08,600
Now, come on, get your trunk.

139
00:09:14,650 --> 00:09:16,310
You better stand back.

140
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:18,850
Let's go.

141
00:09:24,090 --> 00:09:26,330
What was that?

142
00:09:28,430 --> 00:09:30,720
Potter!

143
00:09:30,770 --> 00:09:32,560
Dad, what's going on?

144
00:09:39,770 --> 00:09:41,070
Come on, Harry.

145
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:42,430
Hurry up.

146
00:09:43,880 --> 00:09:46,110
Petunia, he's escaping!

147
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:48,610
I've got you, Harry.

148
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:49,970
Come here!

149
00:09:49,980 --> 00:09:50,910
Let go of me!

150
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:52,210
No, boy!

151
00:09:52,220 --> 00:09:54,810
You and that bloody pigeon aren't going anywhere.

152
00:09:54,820 --> 00:09:56,050
Get off!

153
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:58,150
Drive!

154
00:10:05,030 --> 00:10:07,730
Dad! Are you okey?

155
00:10:21,550 --> 00:10:22,770
By the way, Harry,

156
00:10:22,780 --> 00:10:24,570
happy birthday.

157
00:10:51,750 --> 00:10:53,140
Come on.

158
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:58,010
Okay, come on.

159
00:10:59,090 --> 00:11:00,440
Okay, come on.

160
00:11:09,430 --> 00:11:10,920
Think it'd be all right if we had some?

161
00:11:10,930 --> 00:11:12,630
Yeah, Mum will never know.

162
00:11:30,250 --> 00:11:31,770
It's not much,

163
00:11:31,780 --> 00:11:33,770
but it's home.

164
00:11:33,780 --> 00:11:35,440
I think it's brilliant.

165
00:11:36,660 --> 00:11:40,390
Where have you been?

166
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:41,920
Harry,

167
00:11:41,930 --> 00:11:43,720
how wonderful to see you, dear.

168
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:46,260
Beds empty. No note.

169
00:11:46,270 --> 00:11:49,230
Car gone. You could have died.

170
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:51,130
You could have been seen.

171
00:11:51,140 --> 00:11:53,770
Of course, I don't blame you, Harry, dear.

172
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:55,870
They were starving him, Mum.

173
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:57,440
There were bars on his window.

174
00:11:57,450 --> 00:12:00,400
Well, you best hope I don't put bars on your window,

175
00:12:00,410 --> 00:12:02,080
Ronald Weasley.

176
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:05,070
Come on, Harry, time for a spot of breakfast.

177
00:12:05,520 --> 00:12:08,450
Here we are, Harry. Now, tuck in.

178
00:12:08,460 --> 00:12:11,950
That's it. There we go.

179
00:12:11,990 --> 00:12:13,950
Mummy, have you seen my jumper?

180
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:15,750
Yes, dear, it was on the cat.

181
00:12:16,560 --> 00:12:18,060
Hello.

182
00:12:22,540 --> 00:12:24,030
What did I do?

183
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:26,900
Ginny. She's been talking about you all summer.

184
00:12:26,910 --> 00:12:28,770
A bit annoying, really.

185
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:30,170
Morning, Weasleys.

186
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:32,210
Morning, Dad.

187
00:12:32,450 --> 00:12:33,300
What a night.

188
00:12:33,310 --> 00:12:34,510
Nine raids.

189
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:35,570
Nine!

190
00:12:35,580 --> 00:12:36,610
Raids?

191
00:12:36,620 --> 00:12:38,340
Dad works in the Ministry of Magic,

192
00:12:38,350 --> 00:12:40,640
in the Misuse of Muggle Artifacts Office.

193
00:12:40,650 --> 00:12:41,910
Dad loves Muggles,

194
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:43,850
thinks they're fascinating.

195
00:12:44,060 --> 00:12:45,920
Well, now.

196
00:12:48,230 --> 00:12:49,860
And who are you?

197
00:12:49,860 --> 00:12:50,990
Sorry, sir.

198
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,590
I'm Harry, sir.

199
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:54,200
Harry Potter.

200
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:55,590
Good Lord.

201
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:57,630
Are you really?

202
00:12:57,640 --> 00:13:00,770
Well, Ron has told us all about you,

203
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:01,970
of course. When did he get here?

204
00:13:01,980 --> 00:13:03,740
This morning.

205
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:06,970
Your sons flew that enchanted car of yours to

206
00:13:06,980 --> 00:13:08,940
Surrey and back last night.

207
00:13:08,950 --> 00:13:10,670
Did you really?

208
00:13:10,680 --> 00:13:12,580
-How did it go?  -How useful really...

209
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:13,840
I mean...

210
00:13:13,850 --> 00:13:16,280
That was very wrong indeed, boys.

211
00:13:16,290 --> 00:13:17,960
Very wrong of you.

212
00:13:18,890 --> 00:13:22,690
Now, Harry, you must know all about Muggles.

213
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:23,720
Tell me,

214
00:13:23,730 --> 00:13:27,660
what exactly is the function of a rubber duck?

215
00:13:31,570 --> 00:13:33,460
Well, that'll be Errol with the post.

216
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:41,970
Fetch it, will you, Percy, please?

217
00:13:43,250 --> 00:13:45,540
Errol. He's always doing that.

218
00:13:48,020 --> 00:13:50,350
Look, it's our Hogwarts letters.

219
00:13:50,790 --> 00:13:52,250
They've sent us Harry's as well.

220
00:13:52,260 --> 00:13:53,950
Dumbledore must know you're here.

221
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:55,290
Doesn't miss a trick, that man.

222
00:13:55,300 --> 00:13:57,420
This lot won't come cheap.

223
00:13:57,430 --> 00:13:59,860
The spell books alone are very expensive.

224
00:13:59,870 --> 00:14:01,630
We'll manage.

225
00:14:02,670 --> 00:14:05,030
There's only one place we're going to get all of this.

226
00:14:05,570 --> 00:14:07,200
Diagon Alley.

227
00:14:08,310 --> 00:14:09,540
Right.

228
00:14:09,740 --> 00:14:11,870
Here we are, Harry. You go first, dear.

229
00:14:11,880 --> 00:14:15,010
But Harry's never traveled by Floo powder before, Mum.

230
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:16,240
Floo powder?

231
00:14:16,250 --> 00:14:19,080
You go first, Ron, so that Harry can see how it's done. Yes.

232
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:24,610
In you go. That's it.

233
00:14:28,660 --> 00:14:30,620
Diagon Alley.

234
00:14:36,540 --> 00:14:37,660
You see?

235
00:14:37,670 --> 00:14:39,300
It's quite easy, dear. on't be afraid.

236
00:14:39,310 --> 00:14:40,500
Come on.

237
00:14:41,710 --> 00:14:42,900
Come on.

238
00:14:42,910 --> 00:14:45,330
In you go. That's it. Mind your head.

239
00:14:45,340 --> 00:14:49,580
That's right. Now, take your Floo powder.

240
00:14:51,450 --> 00:14:53,980
That's it, very good.

241
00:14:53,990 --> 00:14:58,250
Now, don't forget to speak very, very clearly.

242
00:15:00,190 --> 00:15:01,720
Diagonally.

243
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,130
What did he say, dear?

244
00:15:10,140 --> 00:15:11,840
Diagonally.

245
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:13,470
I thought he did.

246
00:16:37,630 --> 00:16:40,160
Not lost, are you, my dear?

247
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:42,020
I'm fine, thank you.

248
00:16:42,030 --> 00:16:43,800
I was just going...

249
00:16:44,260 --> 00:16:45,660
Come with us.

250
00:16:45,670 --> 00:16:48,490
We'll help you find your way back.

251
00:16:49,240 --> 00:16:51,500
-No. Please...  -Harry?

252
00:16:51,810 --> 00:16:52,930
Hagrid!

253
00:16:52,940 --> 00:16:54,870
What do you think you're doing down here?

254
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:56,230
Come on.

255
00:17:01,750 --> 00:17:03,370
You're a mess, Harry.

256
00:17:03,380 --> 00:17:05,610
Skulking around Knockturn Alley?

257
00:17:05,620 --> 00:17:07,240
Dodgy place.

258
00:17:07,250 --> 00:17:09,150
Don't want no one to see you there.

259
00:17:09,160 --> 00:17:11,180
People will think you're up to no good.

260
00:17:11,190 --> 00:17:13,790
I was lost, I...

261
00:17:13,860 --> 00:17:16,850
Hang on. What were you doing down there then?

262
00:17:16,860 --> 00:17:17,690
Me?

263
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:19,460
I was...

264
00:17:19,470 --> 00:17:22,160
I was looking for Flesh-Eating Slug Repellent.

265
00:17:22,170 --> 00:17:24,630
They're ruining all the school cabbages.

266
00:17:30,710 --> 00:17:31,840
Harry.

267
00:17:31,850 --> 00:17:32,800
Hagrid.

268
00:17:32,810 --> 00:17:34,610
Hello, Hermione.

269
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:35,870
It's so good to see you.

270
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:37,910
It's great to see you too.

271
00:17:38,020 --> 00:17:40,340
What did you do to your glasses?

272
00:17:40,820 --> 00:17:42,920
Oculus Reparo.

273
00:17:47,190 --> 00:17:49,620
I definitely need to remember that one.

274
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:52,260
You'll be all right now then, Harry?

275
00:17:52,270 --> 00:17:53,020
Right.

276
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:53,990
I'll leave you to it.

277
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,690
-Okay, bye.  -Thank you. Bye.

278
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:57,700
Come on, everyone's been so worried.

279
00:18:08,080 --> 00:18:09,370
Oh, Harry.

280
00:18:09,380 --> 00:18:12,840
Thank goodness. We'd hoped you'd only gone one grate too far.

281
00:18:12,850 --> 00:18:13,940
Ladies and gentlemen,

282
00:18:13,950 --> 00:18:16,150
Mr. Gilderoy Lockhart.

283
00:18:16,160 --> 00:18:17,580
Here he is.

284
00:18:22,230 --> 00:18:24,120
Mum fancies him.

285
00:18:24,130 --> 00:18:25,790
Make way there, please.

286
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:27,490
Let me by, madam. Thank you.

287
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:28,760
Excuse me, little girl.

288
00:18:28,770 --> 00:18:30,870
This is for the Daily Prophet.

289
00:18:35,080 --> 00:18:39,070
It can't be. Harry Potter?

290
00:18:39,550 --> 00:18:41,400
Harry Potter!

291
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:43,040
Excuse me, madam.

292
00:18:44,820 --> 00:18:48,050
Nice big smile, Harry. Together, you and I rate the front page.

293
00:18:48,790 --> 00:18:52,280
Ladies and gentlemen, what an extraordinary moment this is.

294
00:18:52,290 --> 00:18:55,620
When young Harry stepped into Flourish and Blotts this morning...

295
00:18:55,630 --> 00:18:59,630
...to purchase my autobiography, Magical Me...

296
00:19:03,340 --> 00:19:05,630
...which, incidentally, is currently

297
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:11,400
celebrating its 27th week atop the Daily Prophet bestseller list...

298
00:19:11,410 --> 00:19:13,470
he had no idea

299
00:19:13,480 --> 00:19:16,580
that he would, in fact, believing

300
00:19:16,980 --> 00:19:22,090
...with my entire collected works...

301
00:19:22,490 --> 00:19:24,350
...free of charge.

302
00:19:26,960 --> 00:19:29,390
Now ladies...

303
00:19:29,400 --> 00:19:31,360
Harry, now you give me those,

304
00:19:31,370 --> 00:19:32,690
and I'll get them signed.

305
00:19:32,700 --> 00:19:33,990
All of you wait outside.

306
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:35,230
That's it.

307
00:19:45,610 --> 00:19:47,940
I'll bet you loved that, didn't you, Potter?

308
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:49,770
Famous Harry Potter.

309
00:19:49,780 --> 00:19:53,210
Can't even go into a bookshop without making the front page.

310
00:19:53,290 --> 00:19:55,180
Leave him alone.

311
00:19:55,220 --> 00:19:56,510
Look, Potter.

312
00:19:56,520 --> 00:19:58,290
You've got yourself a girlfriend.

313
00:19:58,930 --> 00:20:00,520
Now, now, Draco,

314
00:20:00,530 --> 00:20:01,990
play nicely.

315
00:20:03,260 --> 00:20:05,120
Mr. Potter.

316
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,230
Lucius Malfoy.

317
00:20:09,300 --> 00:20:11,130
We meet at last.

318
00:20:11,140 --> 00:20:12,630
Forgive me.

319
00:20:14,710 --> 00:20:17,300
Your scar is legend.

320
00:20:17,310 --> 00:20:20,010
As, of course, is the wizard who gave it to you.

321
00:20:20,010 --> 00:20:22,840
Voldemort killed my parents.

322
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:26,910
He was nothing more than a murderer.

323
00:20:28,520 --> 00:20:31,720
You must be very brave to mention his name.

324
00:20:32,190 --> 00:20:34,020
Or very foolish.

325
00:20:34,030 --> 00:20:35,890
Fear of a name

326
00:20:35,900 --> 00:20:37,750
only increases fear of the thing itself.

327
00:20:39,070 --> 00:20:41,100
And you must be

328
00:20:41,340 --> 00:20:43,330
Miss Granger.

329
00:20:45,210 --> 00:20:48,200
Yes, Draco has told me all about you.

330
00:20:48,210 --> 00:20:50,200
And your parents.

331
00:20:54,150 --> 00:20:55,870
Muggles,

332
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:57,510
aren't they?

333
00:21:00,450 --> 00:21:01,680
Let me see.

334
00:21:01,690 --> 00:21:03,010
Red hair,

335
00:21:03,020 --> 00:21:05,480
vacant expressions...

336
00:21:07,130 --> 00:21:10,820
...tatty, secondhand book.

337
00:21:10,830 --> 00:21:13,760
You must be the Weasleys.

338
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:16,560
It's mad in here. Let's go outside.

339
00:21:16,570 --> 00:21:19,130
Well, well, well. Weasley senior.

340
00:21:19,210 --> 00:21:20,330
Lucius.

341
00:21:20,340 --> 00:21:22,830
Busy time at the Ministry, Arthur,

342
00:21:22,840 --> 00:21:25,300
all those extra raids?

343
00:21:25,310 --> 00:21:27,770
I do hope they're paying you overtime...

344
00:21:27,780 --> 00:21:29,770
...but judging by the state of this,

345
00:21:29,780 --> 00:21:32,180
I'd say not.

346
00:21:32,820 --> 00:21:35,810
What's the use in being a disgrace to the name of wizard

347
00:21:35,820 --> 00:21:39,050
if they don't even pay you well for it?

348
00:21:39,060 --> 00:21:43,220
We have a very different idea about what disgraces the name of wizard,

349
00:21:43,230 --> 00:21:44,450
Malfoy.

350
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:45,750
Clearly.

351
00:21:48,240 --> 00:21:51,030
Associating with Muggles.

352
00:21:56,180 --> 00:22:00,040
And I thought your family could sink no lower.

353
00:22:03,950 --> 00:22:06,150
I'll see you at work.

354
00:22:10,920 --> 00:22:12,380
See you at school.

355
00:22:21,070 --> 00:22:22,730
10:58. Come on.

356
00:22:22,740 --> 00:22:24,130
The train will be leaving any moment.

357
00:22:24,140 --> 00:22:26,170
Fred, George, Percy, you first.

358
00:22:40,290 --> 00:22:41,680
After you, dear.

359
00:22:44,520 --> 00:22:46,620
Come on, Ginny, we'll get you a seat. Hurry.

360
00:22:48,960 --> 00:22:50,320
Let's go.

361
00:23:03,910 --> 00:23:06,170
What do you two think you're doing?

362
00:23:06,180 --> 00:23:07,740
Sorry.

363
00:23:08,580 --> 00:23:11,110
Lost control of the trolley.

364
00:23:13,090 --> 00:23:14,480
Why can't we get through?

365
00:23:14,490 --> 00:23:17,850
I don't know. The gateway has sealed itself for some reason.

366
00:23:20,190 --> 00:23:21,950
The train leaves at exactly 11 :00.

367
00:23:21,960 --> 00:23:23,350
We've missed it.

368
00:23:24,230 --> 00:23:25,930
Harry,

369
00:23:26,130 --> 00:23:27,890
if we can't get through...

370
00:23:27,900 --> 00:23:30,500
...maybe Mum and Dad can't get back.

371
00:23:31,570 --> 00:23:32,600
Maybe we should

372
00:23:32,610 --> 00:23:34,270
just go and wait by the car.

373
00:23:36,010 --> 00:23:38,140
The car?

374
00:23:48,960 --> 00:23:51,150
Ron, I should tell you...

375
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:54,480
...most Muggles aren't accustomed to seeing a flying car.

376
00:23:54,490 --> 00:23:56,350
Right.

377
00:24:14,850 --> 00:24:16,070
Oh, no!

378
00:24:16,080 --> 00:24:18,540
The lnvisibility Booster must be faulty.

379
00:24:18,550 --> 00:24:20,140
Come on, then. Let's go lower.

380
00:24:20,150 --> 00:24:21,780
We need to find the train.

381
00:24:21,790 --> 00:24:23,060
Okay.

382
00:24:34,270 --> 00:24:36,290
All we need to do is catch up with the train.

383
00:24:36,300 --> 00:24:38,230
We can't be far behind.

384
00:24:40,040 --> 00:24:41,100
Do you hear that?

385
00:24:41,110 --> 00:24:42,970
We must be getting close.

386
00:24:43,240 --> 00:24:44,570
Hold on.

387
00:25:11,440 --> 00:25:13,430
Harry!

388
00:25:16,440 --> 00:25:18,440
Hold on!

389
00:25:21,650 --> 00:25:23,640
Take my hand!

390
00:25:28,420 --> 00:25:29,750
Hold on!

391
00:25:29,760 --> 00:25:31,320
I'm trying.

392
00:25:31,760 --> 00:25:33,790
Your hand's all sweaty.

393
00:25:46,110 --> 00:25:47,360
I think we found the train.

394
00:25:47,370 --> 00:25:48,640
Yeah.

395
00:26:05,930 --> 00:26:07,520
Welcome home.

396
00:26:23,440 --> 00:26:25,140
Up! Up!

397
00:26:25,610 --> 00:26:27,210
It's not working!

398
00:26:32,520 --> 00:26:34,910
Up! Ron, mind that tree!

399
00:26:37,460 --> 00:26:39,730
Stop! Stop! Stop!

400
00:27:02,680 --> 00:27:04,470
My wand.

401
00:27:04,520 --> 00:27:06,040
Look at my wand.

402
00:27:06,050 --> 00:27:07,980
Be thankful it's not your neck.

403
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:11,120
-What's happening?  -I don't know.

404
00:27:47,490 --> 00:27:49,150
Come on, go!

405
00:27:49,160 --> 00:27:50,520
Fast!

406
00:28:23,900 --> 00:28:26,100
Scabbers, you're okay?

407
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:29,460
The car!

408
00:28:45,720 --> 00:28:47,250
Dad's gonna kill me.

409
00:28:56,060 --> 00:28:57,330
See you, Hedwig.

410
00:28:59,830 --> 00:29:02,230
So a house-elf shows up in my bedroom...

411
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:05,230
...we can't get through the barrier to platform 9 3/4...

412
00:29:05,240 --> 00:29:08,030
...we almost get killed by a tree....

413
00:29:08,680 --> 00:29:11,470
Clearly someone doesn't want me here this year.

414
00:29:15,880 --> 00:29:19,020
Well, take a good look, lads.

415
00:29:19,020 --> 00:29:20,580
This night might well be...

416
00:29:20,590 --> 00:29:23,290
the last you spend in this castle.

417
00:29:24,860 --> 00:29:28,530
Oh, dear, we are in trouble.

418
00:29:29,630 --> 00:29:35,300
You were seen by no less than seven Muggles.

419
00:29:36,170 --> 00:29:39,460
Do you have any idea how serious this is?

420
00:29:39,640 --> 00:29:44,330
You have risked the exposure of our world.

421
00:29:44,340 --> 00:29:47,700
Not to mention the damage you inflicted on a Whomping Willow...

422
00:29:47,710 --> 00:29:50,710
...that's been on these grounds since before you were born.

423
00:29:50,720 --> 00:29:52,510
Honestly, Professor Snape,

424
00:29:52,520 --> 00:29:54,280
I think it did more damage to us.

425
00:29:54,290 --> 00:29:55,990
Silence.

426
00:29:57,820 --> 00:29:59,920
I assure you...

427
00:29:59,930 --> 00:30:02,120
that were you in Slytherin,

428
00:30:02,130 --> 00:30:04,290
and your fate rested with me...

429
00:30:04,300 --> 00:30:05,360
...the both of you...

430
00:30:05,370 --> 00:30:09,030
would be on the train home tonight.

431
00:30:09,240 --> 00:30:12,160
-As it is...  -They are not.

432
00:30:13,870 --> 00:30:15,640
Professor Dumbledore.

433
00:30:15,980 --> 00:30:17,500
Professor McGonagall.

434
00:30:18,140 --> 00:30:19,670
Headmaster...

435
00:30:19,680 --> 00:30:21,600
...these boys have flouted

436
00:30:21,610 --> 00:30:25,780
the Decree for the Restriction of Underage Wizardry. As such...

437
00:30:25,790 --> 00:30:26,740
I am well aware of

438
00:30:26,750 --> 00:30:31,750
our bylaws, Severus having written quite a few of them myself.

439
00:30:32,160 --> 00:30:33,320
However,

440
00:30:33,330 --> 00:30:38,190
as head of Gryffindor house it is for Professor McGonagall

441
00:30:38,200 --> 00:30:40,430
to determine the appropriate action.

442
00:30:41,070 --> 00:30:43,290
We'll go and get our stuff, then.

443
00:30:43,300 --> 00:30:45,760
What are you talking about, Mr. Weasley?

444
00:30:45,770 --> 00:30:48,130
You're going to expel us, aren't you?

445
00:30:49,680 --> 00:30:52,540
Not today, Mr. Weasley...

446
00:30:53,010 --> 00:30:55,440
...but I must impress on both of you...

447
00:30:55,450 --> 00:30:58,540
...the seriousness of what you have done.

448
00:30:58,550 --> 00:31:00,940
I will be writing to your families tonight,

449
00:31:00,950 --> 00:31:03,950
and you will both receive detention.

450
00:31:27,650 --> 00:31:29,140
Morning, everyone.

451
00:31:30,780 --> 00:31:33,240
-Good morning, everyone.  -Good morning, Professor Sprout.

452
00:31:33,250 --> 00:31:36,110
Welcome to Greenhouse Three, second years.

453
00:31:36,120 --> 00:31:37,680
Gather around, everyone.

454
00:31:37,820 --> 00:31:40,820
Today we're going to re-pot Mandrakes.

455
00:31:40,830 --> 00:31:44,690
Who here can tell me the properties of the Mandrake root?

456
00:31:44,700 --> 00:31:46,460
Yes, Miss Granger?

457
00:31:47,070 --> 00:31:49,430
Mandrake, or Mandragora...

458
00:31:49,440 --> 00:31:51,900
...is used to return those who have been Petrified

459
00:31:51,910 --> 00:31:54,630
to their original state.

460
00:31:54,640 --> 00:31:56,270
It's also quite dangerous.

461
00:31:56,280 --> 00:31:59,940
The Mandrake's cry is fatal to anyone who hears it.

462
00:31:59,950 --> 00:32:02,840
Excellent. Ten points to Gryffindor.

463
00:32:02,850 --> 00:32:05,510
As our Mandrakes are still only seedlings...

464
00:32:05,520 --> 00:32:07,680
...their cries won't kill you yet.

465
00:32:07,690 --> 00:32:09,250
But they could knock you out for several hours,

466
00:32:09,260 --> 00:32:13,420
which is why I have given you earmuffs for auditory protection.

467
00:32:13,430 --> 00:32:15,690
So could you please put them on, right away?

468
00:32:16,130 --> 00:32:17,560
Quickly.

469
00:32:18,130 --> 00:32:19,420
Flaps tight down,

470
00:32:19,430 --> 00:32:20,860
and watch me closely.

471
00:32:20,870 --> 00:32:24,290
You grasp your Mandrake firmly.

472
00:32:24,300 --> 00:32:27,440
You pull it sharply up out of the pot.

473
00:32:31,510 --> 00:32:33,370
Got it? And...

474
00:32:33,380 --> 00:32:35,970
...now you dunk it down into the other pot...

475
00:32:35,980 --> 00:32:39,140
...and pour a little sprinkling of soil...

476
00:32:39,150 --> 00:32:40,420
...to keep him warm.

477
00:32:44,220 --> 00:32:47,390
Longbottom's been neglecting his earmuffs.

478
00:32:47,890 --> 00:32:50,250
No, ma'am, he's just fainted.

479
00:32:50,260 --> 00:32:51,350
Yes, well,

480
00:32:51,360 --> 00:32:52,220
just leave him there.

481
00:32:52,230 --> 00:32:53,690
Right, on we go.

482
00:32:53,700 --> 00:32:55,990
Plenty of pots to go around.

483
00:32:56,000 --> 00:32:57,890
Grasp your Mandrake

484
00:32:57,900 --> 00:32:59,690
and pull it up.

485
00:33:14,590 --> 00:33:15,850
There's Nearly Headless Nick.

486
00:33:15,860 --> 00:33:17,310
Hello, Percy,

487
00:33:17,320 --> 00:33:18,450
Miss Clearwater.

488
00:33:18,460 --> 00:33:20,160
Hello, Sir Nicholas.

489
00:33:32,470 --> 00:33:33,530
Say it.

490
00:33:33,540 --> 00:33:35,070
I'm doomed.

491
00:33:36,680 --> 00:33:37,770
You don't.

492
00:33:37,780 --> 00:33:39,140
Hi, Harry.

493
00:33:40,810 --> 00:33:41,970
I'm Colin Creevey.

494
00:33:41,980 --> 00:33:43,680
I'm in Gryffindor too.

495
00:33:43,720 --> 00:33:45,880
Hi, Colin. Nice to meet you.

496
00:33:45,950 --> 00:33:48,380
Ron, is that your owl?

497
00:34:02,370 --> 00:34:05,000
Bloody bird's a menace.

498
00:34:09,210 --> 00:34:10,770
Oh, no.

499
00:34:10,910 --> 00:34:12,500
Look, everyone.

500
00:34:12,510 --> 00:34:15,180
Weasley's got himself a Howler.

501
00:34:15,950 --> 00:34:17,040
Go on, Ron.

502
00:34:17,050 --> 00:34:19,740
I ignored one from my gran once.

503
00:34:19,750 --> 00:34:21,540
It was horrible.

504
00:34:28,330 --> 00:34:30,650
Ronald Weasley!

505
00:34:32,800 --> 00:34:35,830
How dare you steal that car!

506
00:34:35,840 --> 00:34:39,100
I am absolutely disgusted!

507
00:34:39,110 --> 00:34:41,900
Your father's now facing an inquiry at work...

508
00:34:41,910 --> 00:34:44,700
...and it's entirely your fault!

509
00:34:44,710 --> 00:34:48,770
If you put another toe out of line...

510
00:34:48,780 --> 00:34:51,550
...we 'll bring you straight home!

511
00:34:52,690 --> 00:34:54,080
And, Ginny, dear,

512
00:34:54,090 --> 00:34:56,380
congratulations on making Gryffindor.

513
00:34:56,390 --> 00:34:59,850
Your father and I are so proud.

514
00:35:18,540 --> 00:35:20,400
Let me introduce you

515
00:35:20,410 --> 00:35:24,740
to your new Defense Against the Dark Arts teacher.

516
00:35:24,980 --> 00:35:26,650
Me.

517
00:35:26,920 --> 00:35:29,480
Gilderoy Lockhart...

518
00:35:29,490 --> 00:35:32,950
...Order of Merlin, Third Class...

519
00:35:32,960 --> 00:35:37,650
...honorary member of the Dark Force Defense League...

520
00:35:37,660 --> 00:35:45,000
...and five times winner of Witch Weekly's Most-Charming-Smile Award.

521
00:35:45,970 --> 00:35:47,560
But I don't talk about that.

522
00:35:47,570 --> 00:35:51,040
I didn't get rid of the Bandon Banshee by smiling at him.

523
00:35:56,020 --> 00:35:57,340
Now,

524
00:35:57,550 --> 00:35:58,980
be warned.

525
00:35:59,050 --> 00:36:01,880
It is my job to arm you...

526
00:36:01,890 --> 00:36:05,880
...against the foulest creatures known to wizardkind.

527
00:36:07,360 --> 00:36:10,990
You may find yourselves facing your worst fears in this room.

528
00:36:11,000 --> 00:36:15,290
Know only that no harm can befall you whilst I am here.

529
00:36:15,300 --> 00:36:18,330
I must ask you not to scream.

530
00:36:18,340 --> 00:36:20,760
It might provoke them.

531
00:36:24,480 --> 00:36:26,240
Cornish pixies?

532
00:36:26,250 --> 00:36:29,310
Freshly caught Cornish pixies.

533
00:36:30,080 --> 00:36:32,340
Laugh if you will, Mr. Finnegan...

534
00:36:32,350 --> 00:36:36,280
...but pixies can be devilishly tricky little blighters.

535
00:36:36,720 --> 00:36:38,450
Let's see what you make of them.

536
00:36:38,460 --> 00:36:40,380
Come on now,

537
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:47,090
round them up. They're only pixies.

538
00:37:05,280 --> 00:37:07,250
Please, get me down!

539
00:37:09,320 --> 00:37:10,710
-Get off me!  -Stop.

540
00:37:10,720 --> 00:37:12,010
Hold still!

541
00:37:13,460 --> 00:37:16,460
Peskipiksi Pesternomi!

542
00:37:36,720 --> 00:37:40,090
I'll ask you three to just nip the rest of them back into their cage.

543
00:37:42,760 --> 00:37:44,490
What do we do now?

544
00:37:46,330 --> 00:37:48,490
Immobulus!

545
00:37:57,370 --> 00:37:59,470
Why is it always me?

546
00:38:06,050 --> 00:38:07,440
I spent the summer devising

547
00:38:07,450 --> 00:38:08,800
a whole new Quidditch program.

548
00:38:08,810 --> 00:38:10,410
We're gonna train earlier,

549
00:38:10,420 --> 00:38:11,370
harder

550
00:38:11,380 --> 00:38:12,650
and longer.

551
00:38:13,990 --> 00:38:15,810
What...? I don't believe it.

552
00:38:18,760 --> 00:38:20,150
Where you think you're going, Flint?

553
00:38:20,160 --> 00:38:21,650
Quidditch practice.

554
00:38:21,660 --> 00:38:23,450
I booked the pitch for Gryffindor today.

555
00:38:23,460 --> 00:38:25,750
Easy, Wood. I've got a note.

556
00:38:27,370 --> 00:38:29,400
I smell trouble.

557
00:38:30,370 --> 00:38:32,130
I, Professor Severus Snape,

558
00:38:32,140 --> 00:38:33,860
do hereby give the Slytherin team...

559
00:38:33,870 --> 00:38:35,600
...permission to practice today,

560
00:38:35,610 --> 00:38:37,570
owing to the need to train their new Seeker.

561
00:38:37,580 --> 00:38:38,800
You've got a new Seeker.

562
00:38:38,810 --> 00:38:40,100
Who?

563
00:38:44,250 --> 00:38:45,540
Malfoy?

564
00:38:45,550 --> 00:38:46,840
That's right.

565
00:38:47,090 --> 00:38:49,010
And that's not all that's new this year.

566
00:38:50,760 --> 00:38:52,950
Those are Nimbus 2001 s.

567
00:38:52,960 --> 00:38:54,250
How did you get those?

568
00:38:54,260 --> 00:38:56,320
A gift from Draco's father.

569
00:38:56,500 --> 00:39:00,520
You see, Weasley, unlike some, my father can afford the best.

570
00:39:00,530 --> 00:39:03,430
At least no one on the Gryffindor team had to buy their way in.

571
00:39:03,440 --> 00:39:05,700
They got in on pure talent.

572
00:39:09,780 --> 00:39:11,900
No one asked your opinion,

573
00:39:11,910 --> 00:39:14,180
you filthy little Mudblood.

574
00:39:15,980 --> 00:39:18,270
You'll pay for that one, Malfoy.

575
00:39:18,280 --> 00:39:19,810
Eat slugs!

576
00:39:27,230 --> 00:39:28,790
You okay, Ron?

577
00:39:32,130 --> 00:39:33,590
Say something.

578
00:39:40,010 --> 00:39:42,030
Wow! Can you turn him around, Harry?

579
00:39:42,040 --> 00:39:43,900
No, Colin, get out of the way.

580
00:39:45,510 --> 00:39:47,210
Let's take him to Hagrid's.

581
00:39:47,750 --> 00:39:49,280
He'll know what to do.

582
00:39:58,020 --> 00:40:01,160
This calls for a specialist's equipment.

583
00:40:05,930 --> 00:40:08,630
Nothing to do but wait till it stops, I'm afraid.

584
00:40:08,630 --> 00:40:11,060
Okay.

585
00:40:11,440 --> 00:40:13,000
Better out than in.

586
00:40:13,770 --> 00:40:15,560
Who was Ron trying to curse, anyway?

587
00:40:15,570 --> 00:40:16,730
Malfoy.

588
00:40:16,740 --> 00:40:20,370
He called Hermione...

589
00:40:20,380 --> 00:40:22,980
Well, I don't know exactly what it means.

590
00:40:27,750 --> 00:40:29,850
He called me a Mudblood.

591
00:40:30,190 --> 00:40:31,650
He did not.

592
00:40:31,660 --> 00:40:33,190
What's a Mudblood?

593
00:40:33,260 --> 00:40:35,020
It means dirty blood.

594
00:40:35,030 --> 00:40:37,750
Mudblood's a really foul name for someone who's Muggle-born.

595
00:40:37,760 --> 00:40:39,690
Someone with non-magic parents.

596
00:40:39,700 --> 00:40:41,760
Someone like me.

597
00:40:42,740 --> 00:40:46,490
It's not a term one usually hears in civilized conversation.

598
00:40:47,910 --> 00:40:49,730
See, the thing is, Harry,

599
00:40:49,740 --> 00:40:51,100
there are some wizards,

600
00:40:51,110 --> 00:40:52,900
like the Malfoy family...

601
00:40:52,910 --> 00:40:57,650
...who think they're better than everyone else because they're pure-blood.

602
00:40:57,820 --> 00:40:59,520
That's horrible.

603
00:41:02,390 --> 00:41:03,850
It's disgusting.

604
00:41:03,860 --> 00:41:06,050
And it's codswallop to boot.

605
00:41:06,060 --> 00:41:07,520
Dirty blood.

606
00:41:07,530 --> 00:41:09,120
Why, there isn't a wizard alive today

607
00:41:09,130 --> 00:41:11,220
that's not half-blood or less.

608
00:41:11,230 --> 00:41:12,820
More to the point, they've yet to

609
00:41:12,830 --> 00:41:15,530
think of a spell that our Hermione can't do.

610
00:41:15,800 --> 00:41:17,500
Come here.

611
00:41:19,240 --> 00:41:22,030
Don't you think on it, Hermione.

612
00:41:22,040 --> 00:41:25,070
Don't you think on it for one minute.

613
00:41:33,490 --> 00:41:36,550
Harry, Harry, Harry.

614
00:41:36,560 --> 00:41:39,010
Can you possibly imagine...

615
00:41:39,020 --> 00:41:45,650
a better way to serve detention than by helping me to answer my fan mail?

616
00:41:45,660 --> 00:41:47,230
Not really.

617
00:41:47,370 --> 00:41:50,360
Fame is a fickle friend, Harry.

618
00:41:50,370 --> 00:41:53,730
Celebrity is as celebrity does.

619
00:41:53,740 --> 00:41:55,400
Remember that.

620
00:41:59,680 --> 00:42:02,000
Come.

621
00:42:02,010 --> 00:42:04,270
Come...

622
00:42:04,280 --> 00:42:08,280
...to me.

623
00:42:08,820 --> 00:42:11,410
Come to me.

624
00:42:11,420 --> 00:42:12,650
What?

625
00:42:12,660 --> 00:42:14,080
Sorry?

626
00:42:16,230 --> 00:42:18,160
That voice.

627
00:42:18,460 --> 00:42:20,200
Voice?

628
00:42:23,470 --> 00:42:25,400
Didn't you hear it?

629
00:42:25,770 --> 00:42:27,900
What are you talking about, Harry?

630
00:42:28,670 --> 00:42:30,430
I think you're getting a bit...

631
00:42:30,440 --> 00:42:32,040
...drowsy.

632
00:42:32,380 --> 00:42:34,900
And great Scott, no wonder. Look at the time.

633
00:42:34,910 --> 00:42:36,910
We've been here nearly four hours.

634
00:42:36,920 --> 00:42:39,780
Spooky how the time flies when one is having fun.

635
00:42:45,190 --> 00:42:47,020
Spooky.

636
00:42:51,460 --> 00:42:53,090
Blood.

637
00:42:53,170 --> 00:42:56,400
I smell blood.

638
00:42:56,700 --> 00:42:59,560
Let me rip you.

639
00:43:00,070 --> 00:43:02,900
Let me kill you.

640
00:43:05,380 --> 00:43:07,510
Kill!

641
00:43:07,950 --> 00:43:11,010
Kill!

642
00:43:11,020 --> 00:43:12,010
Harry!

643
00:43:12,020 --> 00:43:13,410
Did you hear it?

644
00:43:13,420 --> 00:43:14,640
Hear what?

645
00:43:14,650 --> 00:43:15,640
That voice.

646
00:43:15,650 --> 00:43:17,650
Voice? What voice?

647
00:43:18,160 --> 00:43:20,050
I heard it first in Lockhart' s office.

648
00:43:20,060 --> 00:43:21,120
And then again just...

649
00:43:21,130 --> 00:43:22,550
Kill.

650
00:43:22,560 --> 00:43:24,730
It's time.

651
00:43:24,860 --> 00:43:26,690
It's moving.

652
00:43:26,700 --> 00:43:28,730
I think it's going to kill.

653
00:43:28,800 --> 00:43:30,230
Kill?

654
00:43:30,240 --> 00:43:33,440
Harry, wait! Not so fast!

655
00:43:58,400 --> 00:44:00,190
Strange.

656
00:44:01,070 --> 00:44:03,190
I've never seen spiders act like that.

657
00:44:03,200 --> 00:44:04,990
I don't like spiders.

658
00:44:09,640 --> 00:44:11,410
What's that?

659
00:44:15,250 --> 00:44:17,410
The Chamber of Secrets has been opened.

660
00:44:17,420 --> 00:44:19,810
Enemies of the Heir, beware.

661
00:44:19,820 --> 00:44:21,710
It's written in blood.

662
00:44:25,020 --> 00:44:26,620
Oh, no.

663
00:44:32,000 --> 00:44:33,860
It's Filch's cat.

664
00:44:34,870 --> 00:44:36,360
It's Mrs. Norris.

665
00:44:53,020 --> 00:44:55,450
Enemies of the Heir, beware.

666
00:44:57,160 --> 00:44:59,480
You'll be next, Mudbloods.

667
00:44:59,960 --> 00:45:01,350
What's going on here?

668
00:45:01,360 --> 00:45:03,790
Go on. Make way, make way.

669
00:45:06,500 --> 00:45:07,960
Potter?

670
00:45:08,370 --> 00:45:11,400
What are you...?

671
00:45:13,940 --> 00:45:16,070
Mrs. Norris?

672
00:45:17,340 --> 00:45:20,570
You've murdered my cat.

673
00:45:20,580 --> 00:45:22,300
No. No.

674
00:45:22,310 --> 00:45:24,840
I'll kill you.

675
00:45:25,950 --> 00:45:27,710
I'll kill you.

676
00:45:27,720 --> 00:45:29,250
Argus!

677
00:45:30,160 --> 00:45:31,850
How loose sad.

678
00:45:34,330 --> 00:45:35,880
Everyone...

679
00:45:35,890 --> 00:45:39,390
...will proceed to their dormitories immediately.

680
00:45:39,630 --> 00:45:43,890
Everyone except...you three.

681
00:45:46,610 --> 00:45:49,100
Ravenclaws, follow me.

682
00:45:51,000 --> 00:45:53,040
She's not dead, Argus.

683
00:45:53,050 --> 00:45:55,100
She has been Petrified.

684
00:45:55,110 --> 00:45:56,340
Thought so.

685
00:45:56,350 --> 00:45:58,070
So unlucky I wasn't there.

686
00:45:58,080 --> 00:46:01,290
I know exactly the countercurse that could've spared her.

687
00:46:03,690 --> 00:46:06,580
But how she has been Petrified, I cannot say.

688
00:46:06,590 --> 00:46:07,850
Ask him.

689
00:46:07,860 --> 00:46:09,350
It's him that's done it.

690
00:46:09,360 --> 00:46:11,860
You saw what he wrote on the wall.

691
00:46:12,260 --> 00:46:14,690
It's not true, sir. I swear.

692
00:46:14,700 --> 00:46:16,460
I never touched Mrs. Norris.

693
00:46:16,470 --> 00:46:17,760
Rubbish.

694
00:46:17,770 --> 00:46:20,870
If I might, headmaster?

695
00:46:21,410 --> 00:46:23,130
Perhaps Potter and his friends

696
00:46:23,140 --> 00:46:25,670
were simply in the wrong place at the wrong time.

697
00:46:26,810 --> 00:46:28,940
However...

698
00:46:28,950 --> 00:46:32,010
...the circumstances are suspicious.

699
00:46:32,150 --> 00:46:36,880
I, for one, don't recall seeing Potter at dinner.

700
00:46:36,890 --> 00:46:39,280
I'm afraid that's my doing, Severus.

701
00:46:39,290 --> 00:46:42,920
You see, Harry was helping me answer my fan mail.

702
00:46:42,930 --> 00:46:46,620
That's why Ron and l went looking for him, professor.

703
00:46:46,630 --> 00:46:49,560
We'd just found him when he said...

704
00:46:51,540 --> 00:46:53,630
Yes, Miss Granger?

705
00:46:53,640 --> 00:46:56,240
When I said I wasn't hungry.

706
00:46:56,540 --> 00:47:00,070
We were heading back to the common room when we found Mrs. Norris.

707
00:47:02,980 --> 00:47:06,040
Innocent until proven guilty, Severus.

708
00:47:06,050 --> 00:47:09,010
My cat has been Petrified.

709
00:47:09,020 --> 00:47:11,480
I want to see some punishment!

710
00:47:11,490 --> 00:47:15,120
We will be able to cure her, Argus.

711
00:47:16,130 --> 00:47:17,820
As I understand it,

712
00:47:17,830 --> 00:47:19,260
Madam Sprout...

713
00:47:19,270 --> 00:47:20,990
...has a very healthy growth of Mandrake.

714
00:47:21,000 --> 00:47:22,790
When matured, a potion will be made

715
00:47:22,800 --> 00:47:25,700
which will revive Mrs. Norris.

716
00:47:25,870 --> 00:47:28,030
And in the meantime...

717
00:47:28,040 --> 00:47:31,670
...I strongly recommend caution...

718
00:47:32,750 --> 00:47:34,570
...to all.

719
00:47:45,930 --> 00:47:47,660
It's a bit strange, isn't it?

720
00:47:47,990 --> 00:47:49,290
Strange?

721
00:47:49,300 --> 00:47:50,820
You hear this voice,

722
00:47:50,830 --> 00:47:52,390
a voice only you can hear...

723
00:47:52,400 --> 00:47:55,090
...and then Mrs. Norris turns up Petrified.

724
00:47:55,100 --> 00:47:57,290
It's just strange.

725
00:47:57,300 --> 00:47:59,090
Do you think I should have told them?

726
00:47:59,100 --> 00:48:00,460
Dumbledore and the others, I mean?

727
00:48:00,470 --> 00:48:02,230
Are you mad?

728
00:48:02,240 --> 00:48:03,230
No, Harry.

729
00:48:03,240 --> 00:48:04,700
Even in the wizarding world,

730
00:48:04,710 --> 00:48:07,480
hearing voices isn't a good sign.

731
00:48:09,920 --> 00:48:12,240
She's right, you know.

732
00:48:16,490 --> 00:48:18,720
Could I have your attention, please?

733
00:48:19,460 --> 00:48:20,550
Right.

734
00:48:20,560 --> 00:48:22,080
Now, today,

735
00:48:22,090 --> 00:48:24,920
we will be transforming animals...

736
00:48:24,930 --> 00:48:27,100
...into water goblets.

737
00:48:28,430 --> 00:48:29,960
Like so.

738
00:48:30,270 --> 00:48:32,800
One, two, three.

739
00:48:32,810 --> 00:48:34,600
Vera Verto.

740
00:48:38,680 --> 00:48:40,540
Now it's your turn.

741
00:48:40,550 --> 00:48:42,940
Who would like to go first?

742
00:48:42,950 --> 00:48:44,410
Mr. Weasley.

743
00:48:44,420 --> 00:48:45,770
One, two, three.

744
00:48:45,780 --> 00:48:47,480
Vera Verto.

745
00:48:51,760 --> 00:48:53,490
Vera Verto.

746
00:48:59,970 --> 00:49:03,330
That wand needs replacing, Mr. Weasley.

747
00:49:03,870 --> 00:49:04,890
Yes, Miss Granger?

748
00:49:04,900 --> 00:49:06,800
Professor...

749
00:49:06,810 --> 00:49:07,800
...I was wondering if you could tell us...

750
00:49:07,810 --> 00:49:09,570
...about the Chamber of Secrets.

751
00:49:16,650 --> 00:49:18,180
Very well.

752
00:49:19,390 --> 00:49:21,540
You all know, of course...

753
00:49:21,550 --> 00:49:25,510
...that Hogwarts was founded over a thousand years ago...

754
00:49:25,520 --> 00:49:30,320
...by the four greatest witches and wizards of the age

755
00:49:30,400 --> 00:49:32,220
Godric Gryffindor,

756
00:49:32,230 --> 00:49:34,290
Helga Hufflepuff...

757
00:49:34,300 --> 00:49:36,930
...Rowena Ravenclaw

758
00:49:36,940 --> 00:49:39,760
and Salazar Slytherin.

759
00:49:40,410 --> 00:49:46,600
Now, three of the founders coexisted quite harmoniously.

760
00:49:46,610 --> 00:49:48,440
One did not.

761
00:49:48,450 --> 00:49:50,370
Three guesses who.

762
00:49:50,380 --> 00:49:51,940
Salazar Slytherin

763
00:49:51,950 --> 00:49:53,840
wished to be more selective...

764
00:49:53,850 --> 00:49:56,280
...about the students admitted to Hogwarts.

765
00:49:56,290 --> 00:49:57,310
He believed...

766
00:49:57,320 --> 00:50:01,080
...magical learning should be kept within all-magic families.

767
00:50:01,090 --> 00:50:03,620
In other words, pure-bloods.

768
00:50:03,630 --> 00:50:05,820
Unable to sway the others,

769
00:50:05,830 --> 00:50:09,500
he decided to leave the school.

770
00:50:09,840 --> 00:50:12,290
Now, according to legend...

771
00:50:12,300 --> 00:50:16,030
...Slytherin had built a hidden chamber in this castle...

772
00:50:16,040 --> 00:50:19,740
...known as the Chamber of Secrets.

773
00:50:19,880 --> 00:50:22,740
Though, shortly before departing,

774
00:50:22,750 --> 00:50:24,570
he sealed it...

775
00:50:24,580 --> 00:50:28,680
...until that time when his own true Heir returned to the school.

776
00:50:28,690 --> 00:50:31,410
The Heir alone...

777
00:50:31,420 --> 00:50:34,020
...would be able to open the Chamber...

778
00:50:34,030 --> 00:50:37,690
...and unleash the horror within,

779
00:50:37,700 --> 00:50:39,120
and by so doing...

780
00:50:39,130 --> 00:50:42,590
...purge the school of all those who...

781
00:50:42,600 --> 00:50:44,830
...in Slytherin's view,

782
00:50:44,840 --> 00:50:48,230
were unworthy to study magic.

783
00:50:48,310 --> 00:50:50,270
Muggle-borns.

784
00:50:50,680 --> 00:50:55,170
Naturally, the school has been searched many times.

785
00:50:55,180 --> 00:50:58,920
No such chamber has been found.

786
00:50:59,350 --> 00:51:00,640
Professor?

787
00:51:00,650 --> 00:51:02,280
What exactly does legend tell us

788
00:51:02,290 --> 00:51:04,350
lies within the Chamber?

789
00:51:04,760 --> 00:51:07,630
The Chamber is said to be home to something

790
00:51:07,640 --> 00:51:11,490
that only the Heir of Slytherin can control.

791
00:51:11,500 --> 00:51:15,520
It is said to be the home...

792
00:51:15,530 --> 00:51:17,600
...of a monster.

793
00:51:22,910 --> 00:51:24,440
Do you think it's true?

794
00:51:24,510 --> 00:51:26,670
Do you think there really is a Chamber of Secrets?

795
00:51:26,680 --> 00:51:27,640
Yes.

796
00:51:27,650 --> 00:51:28,740
Couldn't you tell?

797
00:51:28,750 --> 00:51:29,910
McGonagall's worried.

798
00:51:29,920 --> 00:51:31,170
All the teachers are.

799
00:51:31,180 --> 00:51:32,840
If there really is a Chamber of Secrets,

800
00:51:32,850 --> 00:51:35,010
and it really has been opened, that means

801
00:51:35,020 --> 00:51:37,310
The Heir of Slytherin has returned to Hogwarts.

802
00:51:37,320 --> 00:51:38,310
The question is,

803
00:51:38,320 --> 00:51:39,450
who is it?

804
00:51:39,460 --> 00:51:40,920
Let's think.

805
00:51:40,930 --> 00:51:42,380
Who do we know who thinks...

806
00:51:42,390 --> 00:51:43,620
...all Muggle-borns are scum?

807
00:51:43,630 --> 00:51:44,820
If you're talking about Malfoy

808
00:51:44,830 --> 00:51:46,460
Of course. You heard him.

809
00:51:46,470 --> 00:51:48,060
You'll be next, Mudbloods.

810
00:51:48,070 --> 00:51:49,220
I heard him.

811
00:51:49,230 --> 00:51:51,130
But Malfoy, the Heir of Slytherin?

812
00:51:51,140 --> 00:51:53,160
Maybe Ron's right, Hermione.

813
00:51:53,170 --> 00:51:54,600
I mean, look at his family.

814
00:51:54,610 --> 00:51:57,530
The whole lot of them have been in Slytherin for centuries.

815
00:51:57,540 --> 00:51:59,270
Crabbe and Goyle must know.

816
00:51:59,280 --> 00:52:01,240
Maybe we could trick them into telling.

817
00:52:01,250 --> 00:52:03,270
Even they aren't that thick.

818
00:52:03,280 --> 00:52:05,640
But there might be another way.

819
00:52:05,780 --> 00:52:07,810
Mind you, it would be difficult.

820
00:52:07,820 --> 00:52:10,980
Not to mention we'd be breaking about 50 school rules...

821
00:52:10,990 --> 00:52:12,880
...and it'll be dangerous.

822
00:52:12,890 --> 00:52:15,280
Very dangerous.

823
00:52:22,800 --> 00:52:23,900
Here it is.

824
00:52:23,910 --> 00:52:25,330
The Polyjuice Potion.

825
00:52:25,340 --> 00:52:26,500
Properly brewed,

826
00:52:26,510 --> 00:52:27,160
the Polyjuice Potion

827
00:52:27,170 --> 00:52:30,240
allows the drinker to transform himself temporarily into...

828
00:52:30,250 --> 00:52:32,640
...the physical form of another.

829
00:52:32,650 --> 00:52:34,710
You mean if Harry and I drink that stuff,

830
00:52:34,720 --> 00:52:35,970
we'll turn into Crabbe and Goyle?

831
00:52:35,980 --> 00:52:36,910
Yeah.

832
00:52:36,920 --> 00:52:37,880
Wicked!

833
00:52:37,890 --> 00:52:39,010
Malfoy will tell us anything.

834
00:52:39,020 --> 00:52:40,250
Exactly.

835
00:52:40,260 --> 00:52:44,320
But it's tricky. I've never seen a more complicated potion.

836
00:52:44,360 --> 00:52:46,550
How long will it take to make?

837
00:52:46,560 --> 00:52:47,750
A month.

838
00:52:47,760 --> 00:52:49,220
A month?

839
00:52:49,460 --> 00:52:51,320
But, Hermione,

840
00:52:51,330 --> 00:52:53,490
if Malfoy is the Heir of Slytherin...

841
00:52:53,500 --> 00:52:56,830
...he could attack half the Muggle-borns in the school by then.

842
00:52:56,840 --> 00:52:58,330
I know.

843
00:52:58,770 --> 00:53:01,540
But it's the only plan we've got.

844
00:53:51,260 --> 00:53:54,430
Another goal for Slytherin!

845
00:53:55,400 --> 00:53:58,500
They lead Gryffindor 90 to 30.

846
00:54:27,800 --> 00:54:30,030
All right there, Scarhead?

847
00:54:36,240 --> 00:54:38,130
Watch yourself, Harry!

848
00:54:39,270 --> 00:54:40,560
Wood, look out!

849
00:54:54,620 --> 00:54:57,520
Blimey! Harry's got himself a rogue Bludger.

850
00:54:57,530 --> 00:55:00,290
That's been tampered with, that has.

851
00:55:00,360 --> 00:55:02,350
I'll stop it.

852
00:55:02,360 --> 00:55:04,920
No! Even with a proper wand, it's too risky.

853
00:55:04,930 --> 00:55:06,670
You could hit Harry.

854
00:55:31,230 --> 00:55:33,520
Training for the ballet, Potter?

855
00:56:05,090 --> 00:56:06,550
You'll never catch me, Potter.

856
00:57:38,090 --> 00:57:39,180
Let's go.

857
00:57:39,190 --> 00:57:42,180
Harry Potter has caught the Snitch.

858
00:57:42,190 --> 00:57:45,050
Gryffindor wins!

859
00:57:50,600 --> 00:57:52,890
Finite Incantatem!

860
00:57:59,810 --> 00:58:01,200
-Thank you.  -Are you okay?

861
00:58:01,210 --> 00:58:03,570
No. I think my arm is broken.

862
00:58:03,580 --> 00:58:06,040
Not to worry, Harry. I will fix that arm of yours straightaway.

863
00:58:06,050 --> 00:58:08,070
No. Not you.

864
00:58:08,080 --> 00:58:10,610
Boy doesn't know what he's saying.

865
00:58:10,620 --> 00:58:14,650
This won't hurt a bit.

866
00:58:20,190 --> 00:58:23,800
Brackium Emendo!

867
00:58:30,440 --> 00:58:32,000
Yes, well,

868
00:58:32,010 --> 00:58:34,430
that can sometimes happen...

869
00:58:34,440 --> 00:58:35,670
...but...

870
00:58:35,680 --> 00:58:38,070
...the point is...

871
00:58:38,310 --> 00:58:39,800
...you can no longer feel any pain,

872
00:58:39,810 --> 00:58:42,340
and, very clearly, the bones are not broken.

873
00:58:42,350 --> 00:58:43,570
Broken?

874
00:58:43,580 --> 00:58:46,010
There's no bones left.

875
00:58:46,720 --> 00:58:48,920
Much more flexible, though.

876
00:58:51,330 --> 00:58:53,850
Mr. Malfoy, stop making such a fuss. You can go.

877
00:58:53,860 --> 00:58:55,520
Out of my way.

878
00:58:55,530 --> 00:58:57,560
Should have been brought straight to me.

879
00:58:57,570 --> 00:58:58,920
I can mend bones in a heartbeat,

880
00:58:58,930 --> 00:59:00,360
but growing them back...

881
00:59:00,370 --> 00:59:01,790
You will be able to, won't you?

882
00:59:01,800 --> 00:59:03,530
I'll be able to, certainly.

883
00:59:03,540 --> 00:59:05,600
But it'll be painful.

884
00:59:05,610 --> 00:59:07,570
You're in for a rough night, Potter.

885
00:59:07,580 --> 00:59:10,500
Regrowing bones is a nasty business.

886
00:59:12,950 --> 00:59:15,650
What do you expect? Pumpkin juice?

887
00:59:22,920 --> 00:59:24,560
Kill.

888
00:59:25,330 --> 00:59:26,720
Kill.

889
00:59:41,910 --> 00:59:43,540
Hello.

890
00:59:44,510 --> 00:59:45,840
Dobby?

891
00:59:45,850 --> 00:59:48,540
Harry Potter should have listened to Dobby.

892
00:59:48,550 --> 00:59:52,280
Harry Potter should have gone back home when he missed the train.

893
00:59:52,290 --> 00:59:54,140
It was you.

894
00:59:54,360 --> 00:59:55,650
You stopped the barrier

895
00:59:55,660 --> 00:59:57,420
from letting Ron and me through.

896
00:59:57,430 --> 00:59:58,350
Indeed.

897
00:59:58,360 --> 01:00:00,130
Yes, sir.

898
01:00:01,400 --> 01:00:03,590
You nearly got Ron and me expelled.

899
01:00:03,600 --> 01:00:06,190
At least you would be away from here.

900
01:00:06,200 --> 01:00:09,330
Harry Potter must go home.

901
01:00:09,340 --> 01:00:10,730
Dobby thought his Bludger...

902
01:00:10,740 --> 01:00:13,100
...would beenough to make Harry Potter see

903
01:00:13,110 --> 01:00:14,230
Your Bludger?

904
01:00:14,240 --> 01:00:16,570
You made that Bludger chase after me?

905
01:00:16,580 --> 01:00:20,470
Dobby feels most aggrieved, sir.

906
01:00:20,480 --> 01:00:24,410
Dobby had to iron his hands.

907
01:00:26,120 --> 01:00:28,590
You better clear off before my bones come back,

908
01:00:28,600 --> 01:00:30,620
Dobby, or I might strangle you.

909
01:00:33,460 --> 01:00:35,520
Dobby is used to death threats, sir.

910
01:00:35,530 --> 01:00:39,060
Dobby gets them five times a day at home.

911
01:00:39,070 --> 01:00:41,890
I don't suppose you could tell me why you're trying to kill me?

912
01:00:41,900 --> 01:00:43,630
Not kill you, sir.

913
01:00:43,640 --> 01:00:45,910
Never kill you.

914
01:00:46,110 --> 01:00:48,600
Dobby remembers how it was before Harry Potter triumphed...

915
01:00:48,610 --> 01:00:54,840
...over He-Who-Must-Not-Be-Named.

916
01:00:54,850 --> 01:00:56,770
We house-elves were treated like vermin, sir.

917
01:00:56,780 --> 01:01:02,020
Of course, Dobby is still treated like vermin.

918
01:01:11,230 --> 01:01:13,930
Why do you wear that thing, Dobby?

919
01:01:14,270 --> 01:01:15,590
This, sir?

920
01:01:15,600 --> 01:01:19,430
It is a mark of the house-elf's enslavement.

921
01:01:19,440 --> 01:01:24,270
Dobby can only be freed if his master presents him with clothes.

922
01:01:26,880 --> 01:01:28,240
Listen.

923
01:01:28,250 --> 01:01:30,010
Listen.

924
01:01:30,020 --> 01:01:34,050
Terrible things are about to happen at Hogwarts.

925
01:01:34,060 --> 01:01:35,310
Harry Potter

926
01:01:35,320 --> 01:01:36,980
must not stay here...

927
01:01:36,990 --> 01:01:41,590
...now that history is to repeat itself.

928
01:01:41,600 --> 01:01:42,990
Repeat itself?

929
01:01:43,000 --> 01:01:45,290
You mean this has happened before?

930
01:01:45,300 --> 01:01:47,500
I shouldn't have said that.

931
01:01:50,870 --> 01:01:52,660
Bad Dobby! Bad!

932
01:01:52,670 --> 01:01:54,070
Dobby.

933
01:01:54,080 --> 01:01:56,070
Stop it! Stop it, Dobby!

934
01:01:57,680 --> 01:01:58,870
Tell me.

935
01:01:58,880 --> 01:02:00,340
When did this happen before?

936
01:02:00,350 --> 01:02:01,610
Who's doing it now?

937
01:02:01,620 --> 01:02:03,740
Dobby cannot say, sir.

938
01:02:03,750 --> 01:02:07,040
Dobby only wants Harry Potter to be safe.

939
01:02:07,050 --> 01:02:10,380
No, Dobby. Tell me. Who is it?

940
01:02:22,000 --> 01:02:23,430
Put him here.

941
01:02:27,480 --> 01:02:28,870
What happened?

942
01:02:28,880 --> 01:02:30,570
There's been another attack.

943
01:02:30,580 --> 01:02:31,900
I think...

944
01:02:31,910 --> 01:02:35,910
...he's been Petrified, Madam Pomfrey.

945
01:02:37,180 --> 01:02:39,110
Look. Perhaps...

946
01:02:39,120 --> 01:02:41,580
...he managed to take a picture of his attacker.

947
01:02:50,030 --> 01:02:52,860
What can this mean, Albus?

948
01:02:52,870 --> 01:02:55,190
It means...

949
01:02:55,200 --> 01:02:58,200
...that our students are in great danger.

950
01:02:58,210 --> 01:03:00,100
What should I tell the staff?

951
01:03:00,110 --> 01:03:01,930
The truth.

952
01:03:01,940 --> 01:03:03,700
Tell them Hogwarts...

953
01:03:03,710 --> 01:03:06,040
...is no longer safe.

954
01:03:06,050 --> 01:03:09,010
It is as we feared, Minerva.

955
01:03:09,020 --> 01:03:13,880
The Chamber of Secrets has indeed been opened again.

956
01:03:16,560 --> 01:03:18,220
Again? You mean...

957
01:03:18,230 --> 01:03:20,790
...the Chamber of Secrets has been opened before?

958
01:03:20,800 --> 01:03:22,090
Of course.

959
01:03:22,100 --> 01:03:23,820
Don't you see?

960
01:03:23,830 --> 01:03:25,690
Lucius Malfoy

961
01:03:25,700 --> 01:03:27,360
must have opened it when he was at school here.

962
01:03:27,370 --> 01:03:29,230
Now he's taught Draco how to do it.

963
01:03:29,240 --> 01:03:30,360
Maybe.

964
01:03:30,370 --> 01:03:33,430
We'll have to wait for the Polyjuice Potion to know for sure.

965
01:03:33,440 --> 01:03:34,530
Enlighten me.

966
01:03:34,540 --> 01:03:37,570
Why are we brewing this potion in broad daylight...

967
01:03:37,580 --> 01:03:39,700
...in the middle of the girls' lavatory?

968
01:03:39,710 --> 01:03:41,780
Don't you think we'll get caught?

969
01:03:42,450 --> 01:03:43,470
No.

970
01:03:43,480 --> 01:03:45,120
No one ever comes in here.

971
01:03:45,920 --> 01:03:47,280
Why?

972
01:03:47,290 --> 01:03:48,680
Moaning Myrtle.

973
01:03:48,690 --> 01:03:50,180
Who?

974
01:03:51,130 --> 01:03:53,080
Moaning Myrtle.

975
01:03:53,090 --> 01:03:54,450
Who's Moaning Myrtle?

976
01:03:54,460 --> 01:03:57,250
I'm Moaning Myrtle.

977
01:04:02,300 --> 01:04:04,560
I wouldn't expect you to know me.

978
01:04:04,570 --> 01:04:06,930
Who would ever talk about ugly,

979
01:04:06,940 --> 01:04:07,970
miserable...

980
01:04:07,980 --> 01:04:11,340
...moping Moaning Myrtle?

981
01:04:18,650 --> 01:04:20,890
She's a little sensitive.

982
01:04:25,430 --> 01:04:27,420
Gather round!

983
01:04:27,700 --> 01:04:28,950
Gather round.

984
01:04:28,960 --> 01:04:32,590
Can everybody see me?

985
01:04:32,600 --> 01:04:35,770
Can you all hear me?

986
01:04:36,670 --> 01:04:37,900
Excellent.

987
01:04:38,440 --> 01:04:42,330
In light of the dark events of recent weeks...

988
01:04:42,340 --> 01:04:47,000
Professor Dumbledore has granted me permission to start this Dueling Club

989
01:04:47,010 --> 01:04:48,510
...to train you all up...

990
01:04:48,520 --> 01:04:50,370
...in case you ever need...

991
01:04:50,380 --> 01:04:52,310
...to defend yourselves...

992
01:04:52,320 --> 01:04:54,710
...as I myself have done on countless occasions.

993
01:04:54,720 --> 01:04:58,510
For full details, see my published works.

994
01:05:03,030 --> 01:05:06,390
Let me introduce my assistant...

995
01:05:06,400 --> 01:05:08,670
...Professor Snape.

996
01:05:12,410 --> 01:05:15,430
He has sportingly agreed to help with a short demonstration.

997
01:05:15,440 --> 01:05:17,500
I don't want any of you youngsters to worry.

998
01:05:17,510 --> 01:05:20,870
You'll still have your Potions master when I'm through with him.

999
01:05:20,880 --> 01:05:22,510
Never fear.

1000
01:05:38,370 --> 01:05:40,060
One.

1001
01:05:40,070 --> 01:05:41,790
Two.

1002
01:05:41,800 --> 01:05:42,630
Three!

1003
01:05:42,640 --> 01:05:45,130
Expelliarmus!

1004
01:05:53,380 --> 01:05:54,740
Do you think he's all right?

1005
01:05:54,750 --> 01:05:56,440
Who cares?

1006
01:05:56,450 --> 01:05:58,140
An excellent idea to show them that,

1007
01:05:58,150 --> 01:06:00,410
Professor Snape but if you don't mind me saying,

1008
01:06:00,420 --> 01:06:02,680
it was pretty obvious...

1009
01:06:02,690 --> 01:06:04,080
what you were about to do.

1010
01:06:04,090 --> 01:06:05,650
If I had wanted to stop you,

1011
01:06:05,660 --> 01:06:07,590
it would have been only too easy.

1012
01:06:07,600 --> 01:06:09,250
Perhaps it would be prudent to first teach the students...

1013
01:06:09,260 --> 01:06:13,720
...to block unfriendly spells,

1014
01:06:13,730 --> 01:06:15,400
professor.

1015
01:06:17,510 --> 01:06:19,900
An excellent suggestion, Professor Snape.

1016
01:06:19,910 --> 01:06:23,030
Let's have a volunteer pair.

1017
01:06:23,040 --> 01:06:25,600
Potter, Weasley, how about you?

1018
01:06:25,610 --> 01:06:29,370
Weasley's wand causes devastation with the simplest spells.

1019
01:06:29,380 --> 01:06:33,110
We'll be sending Potter to the hospital wing in a matchbox.

1020
01:06:33,120 --> 01:06:36,980
Might I suggest someone from my own house?

1021
01:06:38,660 --> 01:06:39,950
Malfoy,

1022
01:06:39,960 --> 01:06:41,450
perhaps?

1023
01:06:48,700 --> 01:06:49,660
Good luck, Potter.

1024
01:06:49,670 --> 01:06:50,940
Thank you, sir.

1025
01:06:59,110 --> 01:07:00,850
Wands at the ready.

1026
01:07:01,780 --> 01:07:03,340
Scared, Potter?

1027
01:07:03,350 --> 01:07:05,140
You wish.

1028
01:07:15,160 --> 01:07:16,850
On the count of three...

1029
01:07:16,860 --> 01:07:19,320
...cast your charms to disarm your opponent.

1030
01:07:19,330 --> 01:07:20,360
Only...

1031
01:07:20,370 --> 01:07:21,530
...to disarm.

1032
01:07:21,540 --> 01:07:24,100
We don't want any accidents here.

1033
01:07:24,210 --> 01:07:25,840
One.

1034
01:07:26,810 --> 01:07:27,800
Two.

1035
01:07:27,810 --> 01:07:29,670
Everte Statum!

1036
01:07:41,020 --> 01:07:42,910
Rictusempra!

1037
01:07:54,300 --> 01:07:56,190
I said disarm only.

1038
01:07:56,200 --> 01:07:57,990
Serpensortia!

1039
01:08:06,750 --> 01:08:08,480
Don' t move, Potter.

1040
01:08:08,480 --> 01:08:09,740
I'll get rid of it for you.

1041
01:08:09,750 --> 01:08:12,310
Allow me, Professor Snape.

1042
01:08:12,490 --> 01:08:15,080
Alarte Ascendare!

1043
01:08:57,900 --> 01:09:01,220
Vipera Evanesca.

1044
01:09:07,270 --> 01:09:09,170
What are you playing at?

1045
01:09:22,390 --> 01:09:23,780
You' re a Parselmouth?

1046
01:09:23,790 --> 01:09:25,120
Why didn't you tell us?

1047
01:09:25,130 --> 01:09:26,020
I'm a what?

1048
01:09:26,030 --> 01:09:27,520
You can talk to snakes.

1049
01:09:27,530 --> 01:09:29,220
I know. I...

1050
01:09:29,230 --> 01:09:32,760
accidentally set a python on my cousin Dudley at the zoo once.

1051
01:09:32,770 --> 01:09:34,190
Once.

1052
01:09:34,200 --> 01:09:35,330
But so what?

1053
01:09:35,340 --> 01:09:37,260
I bet loads of people here can do it.

1054
01:09:37,270 --> 01:09:39,130
No, they can't.

1055
01:09:39,140 --> 01:09:41,500
It's not a very common gift, Harry.

1056
01:09:41,510 --> 01:09:43,030
This is bad.

1057
01:09:43,040 --> 01:09:44,700
What's bad?

1058
01:09:44,710 --> 01:09:46,040
If I hadn't told that snake...

1059
01:09:46,050 --> 01:09:47,470
...not to attack Justin

1060
01:09:47,480 --> 01:09:48,870
That's what you said to it.

1061
01:09:48,880 --> 01:09:50,870
You were there. You heard me.

1062
01:09:50,880 --> 01:09:52,910
I heard you speaking Parseltongue.

1063
01:09:52,920 --> 01:09:54,850
Snake language.

1064
01:09:55,020 --> 01:09:57,810
I spoke a different language?

1065
01:09:58,560 --> 01:10:01,520
But I didn't realize

1066
01:10:01,600 --> 01:10:03,050
How can I speak a language...

1067
01:10:03,060 --> 01:10:04,420
...without knowing I can?

1068
01:10:04,430 --> 01:10:06,090
I don't know, but it sounded like...

1069
01:10:06,100 --> 01:10:08,300
...you were egging the snake on or something.

1070
01:10:08,600 --> 01:10:10,390
Harry, listen to me.

1071
01:10:10,400 --> 01:10:12,360
There's a reason the symbol of Slytherin house is a serpent.

1072
01:10:12,370 --> 01:10:16,600
Salazar Slytherin was a Parselmouth.

1073
01:10:16,610 --> 01:10:18,540
He could talk to snakes too.

1074
01:10:18,550 --> 01:10:19,670
Exactly.

1075
01:10:19,680 --> 01:10:21,140
Now the whole school's gonna think...

1076
01:10:21,150 --> 01:10:23,270
...you're his great-great-great grandson.

1077
01:10:23,280 --> 01:10:25,050
But I'm not.

1078
01:10:28,090 --> 01:10:29,820
I can't be.

1079
01:10:31,090 --> 01:10:33,280
He lived a thousand years ago.

1080
01:10:33,290 --> 01:10:34,650
For all we know,

1081
01:10:34,660 --> 01:10:36,190
you could be.

1082
01:11:06,630 --> 01:11:08,450
I'll see you back in the common room.

1083
01:11:23,440 --> 01:11:30,080
I want blood.

1084
01:11:32,620 --> 01:11:38,220
They all must die.

1085
01:11:38,390 --> 01:11:40,390
Kill.

1086
01:11:40,890 --> 01:11:42,790
Kill.

1087
01:11:43,700 --> 01:11:45,460
Kill.

1088
01:11:46,570 --> 01:11:48,890
Kill.

1089
01:11:48,970 --> 01:11:51,170
Time to kill.

1090
01:12:24,670 --> 01:12:26,630
Caught in the act.

1091
01:12:26,640 --> 01:12:29,130
I'll have you out this time, Potter.

1092
01:12:29,140 --> 01:12:31,840
Mark my words.

1093
01:12:31,850 --> 01:12:33,440
No. Mr. Filch!

1094
01:12:33,450 --> 01:12:35,840
You...you don't understand

1095
01:13:02,880 --> 01:13:04,700
Professor...

1096
01:13:04,910 --> 01:13:06,570
... I swear I didn't.

1097
01:13:06,580 --> 01:13:09,640
This is out of my hands, Potter.

1098
01:13:19,460 --> 01:13:21,920
Professor Dumbledore will be waiting for you.

1099
01:13:30,970 --> 01:13:32,900
Sherbet Lemon.

1100
01:14:07,540 --> 01:14:09,040
Professor Dumbledore.

1101
01:14:26,130 --> 01:14:29,990
Bee in your bonnet, Potter?

1102
01:14:30,700 --> 01:14:32,820
I...

1103
01:14:32,830 --> 01:14:33,860
I was just wondering

1104
01:14:33,870 --> 01:14:36,490
if you put me in the right house.

1105
01:14:36,500 --> 01:14:38,000
Yes.

1106
01:14:38,010 --> 01:14:42,070
You were particularly difficult to place.

1107
01:14:42,080 --> 01:14:45,640
But I stand by what I said last year.

1108
01:14:45,650 --> 01:14:49,240
you would have done well in Slytherin.

1109
01:14:49,250 --> 01:14:50,980
you're wrong.

1110
01:15:19,910 --> 01:15:21,410
Harry?

1111
01:15:21,680 --> 01:15:23,210
Professor.

1112
01:15:23,220 --> 01:15:25,640
your bird...

1113
01:15:25,650 --> 01:15:28,220
There was nothing I could do.

1114
01:15:28,460 --> 01:15:29,980
He just caught fire.

1115
01:15:29,990 --> 01:15:32,650
And about time too.

1116
01:15:32,660 --> 01:15:35,090
He's been looking dreadful for days.

1117
01:15:35,100 --> 01:15:37,890
Pity you had to see him on a burning day.

1118
01:15:39,030 --> 01:15:42,360
Fawkes is a phoenix, Harry.

1119
01:15:42,370 --> 01:15:46,000
They burst into flame when it is time for them to die...

1120
01:15:46,010 --> 01:15:48,200
...and then they are...

1121
01:15:48,210 --> 01:15:51,340
...reborn from the ashes.

1122
01:15:59,750 --> 01:16:02,720
Fascinating creatures, phoenixes.

1123
01:16:02,820 --> 01:16:04,010
They can carry...

1124
01:16:04,020 --> 01:16:06,950
immensely heavy loads.

1125
01:16:06,960 --> 01:16:09,990
Their tears have healing powers.

1126
01:16:12,300 --> 01:16:13,690
Professor Dumbledore, sir!

1127
01:16:13,700 --> 01:16:14,760
Wait!

1128
01:16:14,770 --> 01:16:16,330
Listen!

1129
01:16:16,370 --> 01:16:17,660
Professor Dumbledore, sir,

1130
01:16:17,670 --> 01:16:18,860
it wasn't Harry.

1131
01:16:18,870 --> 01:16:20,530
Hagrid.

1132
01:16:20,540 --> 01:16:21,770
I'd be prepared to swear it in front of the Ministry of Magic.

1133
01:16:21,780 --> 01:16:23,470
Hagrid.

1134
01:16:23,910 --> 01:16:25,640
Relax.

1135
01:16:26,610 --> 01:16:28,610
I do not believe...

1136
01:16:28,750 --> 01:16:31,140
...that Harry attacked anyone.

1137
01:16:31,150 --> 01:16:32,320
Of course you don't.

1138
01:16:34,350 --> 01:16:36,580
Right. Well, I'll...

1139
01:16:36,590 --> 01:16:40,280
I'll just wait outside, then.

1140
01:16:40,290 --> 01:16:41,690
yes.

1141
01:16:45,570 --> 01:16:47,760
you don't think it was me, professor?

1142
01:16:47,770 --> 01:16:49,430
No, Harry.

1143
01:16:49,440 --> 01:16:51,730
I do not think it was you.

1144
01:16:52,970 --> 01:16:55,330
But I must ask you...

1145
01:16:55,340 --> 01:16:59,910
is there something you wish to tell me?

1146
01:17:05,850 --> 01:17:07,350
No, sir.

1147
01:17:07,950 --> 01:17:09,310
Nothing.

1148
01:17:12,430 --> 01:17:13,990
Very well, then.

1149
01:17:14,790 --> 01:17:16,250
Off you go.

1150
01:17:54,530 --> 01:17:55,990
Everything's set.

1151
01:17:56,000 --> 01:17:58,230
We just need a bit of who you're changing into.

1152
01:17:58,240 --> 01:17:59,870
Crabbe and Goyle.

1153
01:18:00,110 --> 01:18:01,570
We also need to make sure...

1154
01:18:01,580 --> 01:18:03,200
that the real Crabbe and Goyle...

1155
01:18:03,210 --> 01:18:06,640
...can't burst in on us while we're interrogating Malfoy.

1156
01:18:06,650 --> 01:18:07,440
How?

1157
01:18:07,450 --> 01:18:09,470
I've got it all worked out.

1158
01:18:09,480 --> 01:18:12,040
I filled these with a simple Sleeping Draught.

1159
01:18:12,050 --> 01:18:15,180
Simple, but powerful.

1160
01:18:15,190 --> 01:18:17,850
Now, once they're asleep...

1161
01:18:17,860 --> 01:18:19,280
...hide them in the broomstick cupboard...

1162
01:18:19,290 --> 01:18:20,820
and pull out a few of their hairs...

1163
01:18:20,830 --> 01:18:22,950
...and put on their uniforms.

1164
01:18:22,960 --> 01:18:24,620
Whose hair are you ripping out, then?

1165
01:18:24,630 --> 01:18:26,320
I've already got mine.

1166
01:18:26,330 --> 01:18:28,360
Millicent Bulstrode.

1167
01:18:28,370 --> 01:18:29,660
Slytherin.

1168
01:18:29,670 --> 01:18:32,100
I got this off her robes.

1169
01:18:32,110 --> 01:18:34,800
I'm going to go check on the Polyjuice Potion.

1170
01:18:34,810 --> 01:18:38,100
Make sure that Crabbe and Goyle find these.

1171
01:18:48,920 --> 01:18:52,450
Ron, maybe I should do it.

1172
01:18:52,460 --> 01:18:53,850
Yeah. Right.

1173
01:18:56,560 --> 01:18:58,460
Wingardium Leviosa.

1174
01:19:08,970 --> 01:19:10,930
Cool.

1175
01:19:33,270 --> 01:19:35,290
How thick could you get?

1176
01:19:35,300 --> 01:19:36,760
Come on, let's get them.

1177
01:19:40,040 --> 01:19:41,530
We'll have exactly one hour

1178
01:19:41,540 --> 01:19:43,210
before we change back into ourselves.

1179
01:19:52,120 --> 01:19:53,650
Add the hairs.

1180
01:19:58,660 --> 01:20:00,580
Essence of Crabbe.

1181
01:20:00,590 --> 01:20:01,990
Cheers.

1182
01:20:11,100 --> 01:20:13,030
I think I'm gonna be sick.

1183
01:20:16,440 --> 01:20:17,940
Me too.

1184
01:21:03,090 --> 01:21:04,580
Harry?

1185
01:21:05,390 --> 01:21:06,820
Ron.

1186
01:21:07,730 --> 01:21:09,490
Bloody hell!

1187
01:21:10,530 --> 01:21:12,920
We still sound like ourselves.

1188
01:21:13,030 --> 01:21:15,060
You need to sound more like Crabbe.

1189
01:21:15,070 --> 01:21:17,460
Bloody hell.

1190
01:21:17,640 --> 01:21:18,660
Excellent.

1191
01:21:18,670 --> 01:21:20,260
But where's Hermione?

1192
01:21:20,270 --> 01:21:21,300
I...

1193
01:21:21,310 --> 01:21:23,030
I don't think I'm going.

1194
01:21:23,040 --> 01:21:24,600
You go on without me.

1195
01:21:24,610 --> 01:21:26,300
Hermione, are you okay?

1196
01:21:26,310 --> 01:21:27,300
Just go.

1197
01:21:27,310 --> 01:21:29,140
You're wasting time.

1198
01:21:31,220 --> 01:21:32,480
Come on.

1199
01:21:36,390 --> 01:21:38,250
I think the Slytherin common room's this way.

1200
01:21:38,260 --> 01:21:39,490
Okay.

1201
01:21:42,760 --> 01:21:44,650
Excuse me.

1202
01:21:46,830 --> 01:21:48,730
What are you doing...?

1203
01:21:49,140 --> 01:21:51,930
I mean, what are you doing down here?

1204
01:21:53,070 --> 01:21:55,970
I happen to be a school prefect.

1205
01:21:55,980 --> 01:21:58,070
you, on the other hand,

1206
01:21:58,080 --> 01:22:00,850
have no business wandering the corridors at night.

1207
01:22:01,050 --> 01:22:02,470
What are your names again?

1208
01:22:02,480 --> 01:22:04,440
I'm...

1209
01:22:04,450 --> 01:22:05,680
Crabbe, Goyle,

1210
01:22:05,690 --> 01:22:07,180
where have you two been?

1211
01:22:07,190 --> 01:22:10,190
Pigging out in the Great Hall all this time?

1212
01:22:11,720 --> 01:22:13,820
Why are you wearing glasses?

1213
01:22:13,830 --> 01:22:16,050
Reading.

1214
01:22:16,060 --> 01:22:17,890
Reading?

1215
01:22:18,930 --> 01:22:21,060
I didn't know you could read.

1216
01:22:24,070 --> 01:22:26,260
And what are you doing down here, Weasley?

1217
01:22:26,270 --> 01:22:29,440
Mind your attitude, Malfoy.

1218
01:22:37,120 --> 01:22:38,640
Well, sit down.

1219
01:22:41,920 --> 01:22:44,410
You'd never know the Weasleys were pure-bloods,

1220
01:22:44,420 --> 01:22:45,980
the way they behave.

1221
01:22:45,990 --> 01:22:48,150
They're an embarrassment to the wizarding world.

1222
01:22:48,160 --> 01:22:49,660
All of them.

1223
01:22:50,700 --> 01:22:52,690
What's wrong with you, Crabbe?

1224
01:22:55,200 --> 01:22:56,970
Stomachache.

1225
01:22:58,870 --> 01:22:59,900
you know,

1226
01:22:59,910 --> 01:23:01,630
I'm surprised the Daily Prophet

1227
01:23:01,640 --> 01:23:03,870
hasn't done a report on all these attacks.

1228
01:23:03,880 --> 01:23:06,740
I suppose Dumbledore is trying to hush it all up.

1229
01:23:06,750 --> 01:23:08,570
Father always said Dumbledore was the worst thing...

1230
01:23:08,580 --> 01:23:10,940
...that ever happened to this place.

1231
01:23:10,950 --> 01:23:12,340
You're wrong!

1232
01:23:20,560 --> 01:23:21,920
What?

1233
01:23:21,930 --> 01:23:23,020
You think...

1234
01:23:23,030 --> 01:23:25,230
...there's someone here who's worse than Dumbledore?

1235
01:23:25,600 --> 01:23:27,890
Well? Do you?

1236
01:23:28,600 --> 01:23:30,330
Harry Potter?

1237
01:23:37,040 --> 01:23:38,640
Good one, Goyle.

1238
01:23:38,680 --> 01:23:40,810
You're absolutely right.

1239
01:23:40,880 --> 01:23:43,080
Saint Potter.

1240
01:23:43,750 --> 01:23:45,110
And people

1241
01:23:45,120 --> 01:23:47,350
actually think that he's the Heir of Slytherin?

1242
01:23:50,360 --> 01:23:53,020
But then you must have some idea who's behind it all.

1243
01:23:53,030 --> 01:23:56,300
You know I don't, Goyle. I told you yesterday.

1244
01:23:57,630 --> 01:23:59,450
How many times do I have to tell you?

1245
01:24:01,200 --> 01:24:03,020
Is this yours?

1246
01:24:07,540 --> 01:24:10,210
But my father did say this.

1247
01:24:10,310 --> 01:24:13,400
It's been 50 years since the Chamber was opened.

1248
01:24:13,410 --> 01:24:15,240
He wouldn't tell me who opened it.

1249
01:24:15,250 --> 01:24:17,540
Only that they were expelled.

1250
01:24:18,020 --> 01:24:20,640
The last time the Chamber of Secrets was opened,

1251
01:24:20,650 --> 01:24:22,480
a Mudblood died.

1252
01:24:22,890 --> 01:24:24,550
So it's only a matter of time

1253
01:24:24,560 --> 01:24:26,790
before one of them is killed this time.

1254
01:24:27,790 --> 01:24:29,790
As for me...

1255
01:24:29,800 --> 01:24:31,790
...I hope it's Granger.

1256
01:24:32,270 --> 01:24:34,260
What's the matter with you two?

1257
01:24:34,500 --> 01:24:37,160
you're acting very odd.

1258
01:24:37,170 --> 01:24:39,530
It's his stomachache.

1259
01:24:39,540 --> 01:24:41,200
Calm down.

1260
01:24:45,310 --> 01:24:47,410
Scar.

1261
01:24:51,250 --> 01:24:52,950
Hair.

1262
01:24:58,660 --> 01:25:00,760
Hey! Where are you going?

1263
01:25:04,360 --> 01:25:05,760
That was close.

1264
01:25:05,770 --> 01:25:08,260
Hermione, come out. We've got loads to tell you.

1265
01:25:08,270 --> 01:25:09,760
Go away.

1266
01:25:09,840 --> 01:25:12,400
Wait till you see.

1267
01:25:12,410 --> 01:25:14,100
It's awful.

1268
01:25:16,680 --> 01:25:20,000
Hermione? Are you okay?

1269
01:25:22,220 --> 01:25:24,110
Do you remember me telling you...

1270
01:25:24,120 --> 01:25:27,440
...that the Polyjuice Potion was only for human transformations?

1271
01:25:27,450 --> 01:25:31,290
It was cat hair I plucked off Millicent Bulstrode's robes.

1272
01:25:34,030 --> 01:25:35,920
Look at my face.

1273
01:25:36,760 --> 01:25:38,550
Look at your tail.

1274
01:25:45,640 --> 01:25:47,200
Have you spoken to Hermione?

1275
01:25:47,210 --> 01:25:49,930
She should be out of hospital in a few days...

1276
01:25:49,940 --> 01:25:52,400
...when she stops coughing up fur balls.

1277
01:25:57,650 --> 01:25:59,280
What's this?

1278
01:26:03,960 --> 01:26:05,210
Yuck!

1279
01:26:05,220 --> 01:26:08,150
Looks like Moaning Myrtle's flooded the bathroom.

1280
01:26:24,210 --> 01:26:26,640
Come to throw something else at me?

1281
01:26:26,650 --> 01:26:28,740
Why would I throw something at you?

1282
01:26:28,750 --> 01:26:30,510
Don't ask me.

1283
01:26:30,520 --> 01:26:31,700
Here I am,

1284
01:26:31,710 --> 01:26:36,850
minding my own business and someone thinks it's funny to throw a book at me.

1285
01:26:36,860 --> 01:26:39,880
But it can't hurt if someone throws something at you.

1286
01:26:39,890 --> 01:26:40,920
I mean,

1287
01:26:40,930 --> 01:26:42,690
it'll just go right through you.

1288
01:26:43,430 --> 01:26:47,890
Sure! Let's all throw books at Myrtle because she can't feel it.

1289
01:26:47,900 --> 01:26:50,690
Ten points if you get it through her stomach!

1290
01:26:50,700 --> 01:26:53,670
Fifty points if it goes through her head!

1291
01:26:54,740 --> 01:26:56,500
But who threw it at you, anyway?

1292
01:26:56,510 --> 01:26:57,600
I don't know.

1293
01:26:57,610 --> 01:26:59,400
I didn't see them.

1294
01:26:59,410 --> 01:27:01,500
I was just sitting in the U-bend,

1295
01:27:01,510 --> 01:27:03,140
thinking about death...

1296
01:27:03,150 --> 01:27:04,940
...and it fell...

1297
01:27:04,950 --> 01:27:07,520
...through the top of my head.

1298
01:27:37,820 --> 01:27:40,980
Tom Marvolo Riddle

1299
01:28:10,150 --> 01:28:13,980
My name...

1300
01:28:13,990 --> 01:28:16,220
...is Harry...

1301
01:28:16,760 --> 01:28:18,520
...Potter.

1302
01:28:32,540 --> 01:28:40,300
Do you know anything... ...about the Chamber of Secrets?

1303
01:28:55,260 --> 01:28:58,020
Can you...

1304
01:28:58,030 --> 01:29:00,800
...tell me?

1305
01:30:03,100 --> 01:30:04,650
Excuse me.

1306
01:30:04,660 --> 01:30:07,060
Could you tell me what's going on here?

1307
01:30:09,940 --> 01:30:11,760
Are you Tom Riddle?

1308
01:30:12,470 --> 01:30:14,400
Hello, can you hear me?

1309
01:30:34,830 --> 01:30:36,220
Riddle!

1310
01:30:37,160 --> 01:30:38,660
Come.

1311
01:30:38,970 --> 01:30:40,490
Professor Dumbledore.

1312
01:30:42,940 --> 01:30:44,860
Dumbledore?

1313
01:30:46,510 --> 01:30:49,870
It is not wise to be wandering around this late hour, Tom.

1314
01:30:49,880 --> 01:30:51,270
Yes, professor.

1315
01:30:51,580 --> 01:30:53,640
I suppose I....

1316
01:30:53,650 --> 01:30:56,370
I had to see for myself if the rumors were true.

1317
01:30:56,380 --> 01:30:59,520
I'm afraid they are, Tom. They are true.

1318
01:30:59,520 --> 01:31:01,380
About the school as well?

1319
01:31:01,650 --> 01:31:02,710
I don't have a home to go to.

1320
01:31:02,720 --> 01:31:05,380
They wouldn't really close Hogwarts, would they, professor?

1321
01:31:05,390 --> 01:31:07,150
I understand, Tom,

1322
01:31:07,160 --> 01:31:08,820
but I'm afraid...

1323
01:31:08,830 --> 01:31:11,790
...Headmaster Dippet may have no choice.

1324
01:31:11,930 --> 01:31:13,490
Sir, if it all stopped,

1325
01:31:13,500 --> 01:31:16,770
if the person responsible was caught....

1326
01:31:18,800 --> 01:31:21,570
Is there something...

1327
01:31:21,710 --> 01:31:24,130
...you wish to tell me?

1328
01:31:24,940 --> 01:31:26,400
No, sir.

1329
01:31:26,410 --> 01:31:27,770
Nothing.

1330
01:31:34,350 --> 01:31:35,810
Very well, then.

1331
01:31:36,120 --> 01:31:37,510
Off you go.

1332
01:31:37,520 --> 01:31:38,880
Good night, sir.

1333
01:32:15,360 --> 01:32:16,290
Let's get you out of there.

1334
01:32:16,300 --> 01:32:17,760
Evening, Hagrid.

1335
01:32:18,730 --> 01:32:20,920
I'm going to have to turn you in, Hagrid.

1336
01:32:20,930 --> 01:32:23,160
I don't think you meant it to kill anyone....

1337
01:32:23,170 --> 01:32:24,260
You can't.

1338
01:32:24,270 --> 01:32:25,900
You don't understand.

1339
01:32:25,910 --> 01:32:27,630
The dead girl's parents will be here tomorrow.

1340
01:32:27,640 --> 01:32:29,070
The least Hogwarts can do...

1341
01:32:29,080 --> 01:32:32,170
...is make sure the thing that killed their daughter is slaughtered.

1342
01:32:32,180 --> 01:32:33,370
It wasn't him.

1343
01:32:33,380 --> 01:32:35,570
Aragog never killed no one. Never.

1344
01:32:35,580 --> 01:32:37,750
Monsters don't make good pets, Hagrid.

1345
01:32:38,020 --> 01:32:39,580
-Now, stand aside.  -No!

1346
01:32:39,590 --> 01:32:40,980
Stand aside, Hagrid.

1347
01:32:40,990 --> 01:32:41,880
No!

1348
01:32:41,890 --> 01:32:43,920
Cistem Aperio!

1349
01:32:50,460 --> 01:32:52,460
Arania Exumai!

1350
01:32:53,670 --> 01:32:56,490
Aragog!

1351
01:32:57,040 --> 01:32:59,030
I can't let you go.

1352
01:32:59,040 --> 01:33:03,400
They'll have your wand for this, Hagrid. You'll be expelled.

1353
01:33:04,810 --> 01:33:06,600
Hagrid!

1354
01:33:12,250 --> 01:33:15,490
Hagrid!

1355
01:33:36,840 --> 01:33:38,000
It was Hagrid.

1356
01:33:38,010 --> 01:33:41,000
Hagrid opened the Chamber of Secrets 50 years ago.

1357
01:33:41,010 --> 01:33:42,340
It can't be Hagrid.

1358
01:33:42,350 --> 01:33:44,140
It just can't be.

1359
01:33:44,150 --> 01:33:45,980
We don't even know this Tom Riddle.

1360
01:33:45,990 --> 01:33:48,410
He sounds like a dirty, rotten snitch to me.

1361
01:33:48,420 --> 01:33:50,510
The monster had killed somebody, Ron.

1362
01:33:50,520 --> 01:33:52,210
What would any of us have done?

1363
01:33:52,220 --> 01:33:54,250
Look, Hagrid's our friend.

1364
01:33:54,260 --> 01:33:56,390
Why don't we just go and ask him about it?

1365
01:33:56,400 --> 01:33:58,220
That would be a cheerful visit.

1366
01:33:58,230 --> 01:33:59,220
Hello, Hagrid.

1367
01:33:59,230 --> 01:34:01,820
Tell us, have you been setting anything

1368
01:34:01,830 --> 01:34:03,230
mad and hairy loose in the castle lately?

1369
01:34:03,240 --> 01:34:04,730
Mad and hairy?

1370
01:34:04,740 --> 01:34:06,700
You wouldn't be talking about me, now, would you?

1371
01:34:06,710 --> 01:34:08,300
No.

1372
01:34:12,310 --> 01:34:14,370
What's that you've got, Hagrid?

1373
01:34:14,580 --> 01:34:17,470
It's Flesh-Eating Slug Repellent.

1374
01:34:17,480 --> 01:34:18,810
For the Mandrakes, you know.

1375
01:34:18,820 --> 01:34:20,880
Now, according to Professor Sprout,

1376
01:34:20,890 --> 01:34:22,480
they've still got a bit of growing up to do.

1377
01:34:22,490 --> 01:34:24,480
But once their acne's cleared up,

1378
01:34:24,490 --> 01:34:26,650
we'll be able to chop them up and stew them...

1379
01:34:26,660 --> 01:34:30,690
...and then we'll get those people down at the hospital un-Petrified.

1380
01:34:31,400 --> 01:34:32,760
In the meantime, though,

1381
01:34:32,770 --> 01:34:34,490
you three...

1382
01:34:34,500 --> 01:34:36,960
...had best be looking after yourselves.

1383
01:34:36,970 --> 01:34:38,530
All right?

1384
01:34:45,710 --> 01:34:47,040
Hello, Neville.

1385
01:34:48,510 --> 01:34:50,210
Harry, I don't know who did it,

1386
01:34:50,220 --> 01:34:51,470
but you'd better come.

1387
01:34:51,480 --> 01:34:52,720
Come on!

1388
01:35:15,670 --> 01:35:17,200
It had to be a Gryffindor.

1389
01:35:17,210 --> 01:35:19,880
Nobody else knows our password.

1390
01:35:19,950 --> 01:35:22,270
Unless it wasn't a student.

1391
01:35:22,310 --> 01:35:23,610
Whoever it was,

1392
01:35:23,620 --> 01:35:25,750
they must have been looking for something.

1393
01:35:26,020 --> 01:35:28,010
And they found it.

1394
01:35:28,020 --> 01:35:30,250
Tom Riddle's diary is gone.

1395
01:35:32,120 --> 01:35:33,620
All right, listen up.

1396
01:35:33,630 --> 01:35:35,020
We play our game,

1397
01:35:35,030 --> 01:35:36,690
Hufflepuff doesn't stand a chance.

1398
01:35:36,860 --> 01:35:38,690
We're stronger, quicker and smarter.

1399
01:35:38,700 --> 01:35:40,660
Not to mention they're dead scared that Harry will Petrify them...

1400
01:35:40,670 --> 01:35:43,460
...if they fly anywhere near him.

1401
01:35:43,470 --> 01:35:44,760
Well, that too.

1402
01:35:46,710 --> 01:35:48,300
Professor McGonagall.

1403
01:35:48,310 --> 01:35:50,230
This match has been canceled.

1404
01:35:50,240 --> 01:35:51,430
We can't cancel Quidditch.

1405
01:35:51,440 --> 01:35:52,740
Silence, Wood.

1406
01:35:52,750 --> 01:35:54,140
You and your teammates

1407
01:35:54,150 --> 01:35:56,470
will go to Gryffindor Tower. Now.

1408
01:35:56,480 --> 01:35:59,640
Potter, you and I will find Mr. Weasley.

1409
01:35:59,650 --> 01:36:02,750
There's something the both of you have to see.

1410
01:36:04,360 --> 01:36:07,780
I warn you. This could be a wee bit of a shock.

1411
01:36:16,370 --> 01:36:17,690
Hermione!

1412
01:36:17,700 --> 01:36:20,160
She was found near the library...

1413
01:36:20,670 --> 01:36:22,670
...along with this.

1414
01:36:24,210 --> 01:36:26,670
Does it mean anything to either of you?

1415
01:36:27,280 --> 01:36:28,710
No.

1416
01:36:42,960 --> 01:36:45,090
Could I have your attention, please?

1417
01:36:45,100 --> 01:36:46,860
Because of recent events,

1418
01:36:46,870 --> 01:36:50,730
these new rules will be put into effect immediately.

1419
01:36:51,340 --> 01:36:54,100
All students will return to their house common rooms by 6:00 every evening.

1420
01:36:56,610 --> 01:36:58,400
All students

1421
01:36:58,410 --> 01:37:00,900
will be escorted to each lesson by a teacher.

1422
01:37:00,910 --> 01:37:03,580
No exceptions.

1423
01:37:04,580 --> 01:37:06,810
I should tell you this,

1424
01:37:06,820 --> 01:37:11,110
behind these attacks is caught Unless the culprit...

1425
01:37:11,460 --> 01:37:14,520
...it is likely the school will be closed.

1426
01:37:26,170 --> 01:37:28,160
We've got to talk to Hagrid, Ron.

1427
01:37:28,170 --> 01:37:29,400
I can't believe it's him...

1428
01:37:29,410 --> 01:37:31,600
...but if he did set the monster loose last time...

1429
01:37:31,610 --> 01:37:33,900
...he'll know how to get inside the Chamber of Secrets.

1430
01:37:33,910 --> 01:37:35,070
That's a start.

1431
01:37:35,080 --> 01:37:36,470
But you heard McGonagall.

1432
01:37:36,480 --> 01:37:39,550
We're not allowed to leave the tower except for class.

1433
01:37:40,250 --> 01:37:43,020
I think it's time to get my dad's old cloak out again.

1434
01:37:56,540 --> 01:37:57,930
Who's there?

1435
01:38:01,910 --> 01:38:03,200
Hello?

1436
01:38:04,080 --> 01:38:05,470
Hello?

1437
01:38:06,550 --> 01:38:07,970
What's that for?

1438
01:38:07,980 --> 01:38:11,170
Nothing. I was expecting....

1439
01:38:11,180 --> 01:38:12,540
It doesn't matter.

1440
01:38:12,550 --> 01:38:13,410
Come on in.

1441
01:38:13,420 --> 01:38:15,020
I just made a pot of tea.

1442
01:38:17,860 --> 01:38:18,850
Hagrid,

1443
01:38:18,860 --> 01:38:20,250
are you okay?

1444
01:38:20,360 --> 01:38:21,620
I'm fine.

1445
01:38:21,630 --> 01:38:23,050
I'm all right.

1446
01:38:23,960 --> 01:38:26,460
Did you hear about Hermione?

1447
01:38:26,470 --> 01:38:29,460
Yeah. I heard about that, all right.

1448
01:38:30,370 --> 01:38:31,630
Look,

1449
01:38:31,640 --> 01:38:33,670
we have to ask you something.

1450
01:38:35,710 --> 01:38:38,870
Do you know who's opened the Chamber of Secrets?

1451
01:38:41,510 --> 01:38:44,010
What you had to understand about that is...

1452
01:38:45,550 --> 01:38:47,840
Quick, under the cloak.

1453
01:38:47,850 --> 01:38:50,420
Don't say a word. Be quiet, both of you.

1454
01:38:57,300 --> 01:38:58,650
Professor Dumbledore, sir.

1455
01:38:58,660 --> 01:39:00,560
Good evening, Hagrid.

1456
01:39:00,570 --> 01:39:02,420
I wonder,

1457
01:39:02,430 --> 01:39:03,830
-could we...?  -Of course.

1458
01:39:03,840 --> 01:39:05,360
Come in. Come in.

1459
01:39:05,840 --> 01:39:07,400
That's Dad's boss.

1460
01:39:07,410 --> 01:39:09,260
Cornelius Fudge,

1461
01:39:09,270 --> 01:39:11,100
Minister of Magic.

1462
01:39:11,110 --> 01:39:12,500
Bad business, Hagrid,

1463
01:39:12,510 --> 01:39:14,470
very bad business.

1464
01:39:14,480 --> 01:39:15,800
Had to come.

1465
01:39:15,810 --> 01:39:19,040
Three attacks on Muggle-borns. Things have gone far enough.

1466
01:39:19,050 --> 01:39:21,310
The Ministry's got to act.

1467
01:39:21,320 --> 01:39:23,580
But I never...you know I never, professor.

1468
01:39:23,590 --> 01:39:27,550
I want it understood, Cornelius...

1469
01:39:27,730 --> 01:39:29,690
...that Hagrid...

1470
01:39:29,700 --> 01:39:32,150
...has my full confidence.

1471
01:39:32,160 --> 01:39:33,220
Albus, look,

1472
01:39:33,230 --> 01:39:37,630
Hagrid's record is against him. I've got to take him.

1473
01:39:37,640 --> 01:39:39,660
Take me? Take me where?

1474
01:39:39,670 --> 01:39:41,430
Not Azkaban prison.

1475
01:39:41,440 --> 01:39:44,900
I'm afraid we have no choice, Hagrid.

1476
01:39:45,880 --> 01:39:47,700
Already here, Fudge?

1477
01:39:47,880 --> 01:39:49,150
Good.

1478
01:39:50,080 --> 01:39:51,510
What are you doing here?

1479
01:39:51,520 --> 01:39:53,310
Get out of my house!

1480
01:39:53,590 --> 01:39:55,340
Believe me...

1481
01:39:55,350 --> 01:39:58,990
...I take absolutely no pleasure being inside your...

1482
01:40:01,530 --> 01:40:03,260
you call this a house?

1483
01:40:06,000 --> 01:40:07,290
I simply called up the school

1484
01:40:07,300 --> 01:40:09,500
and was told the headmaster was here.

1485
01:40:09,970 --> 01:40:14,590
Well, what exactly is it that you want with me?

1486
01:40:14,600 --> 01:40:17,590
The other governors and I have decided...

1487
01:40:17,600 --> 01:40:20,380
...it's time for you to step aside.

1488
01:40:21,080 --> 01:40:23,400
This is an order of suspension.

1489
01:40:29,550 --> 01:40:32,120
You'll find all 1 2 signatures on it.

1490
01:40:36,760 --> 01:40:41,330
I'm afraid we feel you've rather lost your touch.

1491
01:40:41,800 --> 01:40:44,260
Well, what, with all these attacks...

1492
01:40:44,270 --> 01:40:48,000
...there'll be no Muggle-borns left at Hogwarts.

1493
01:40:48,010 --> 01:40:51,540
I can only imagine what an awful loss that would be to the school.

1494
01:40:51,740 --> 01:40:54,340
you can't take Professor Dumbledore away.

1495
01:40:54,350 --> 01:40:56,970
Take him away and the Muggle-borns won't stand a chance.

1496
01:40:56,980 --> 01:40:59,550
You mark my words, there'll be killings next!

1497
01:40:59,790 --> 01:41:01,510
You think so?

1498
01:41:01,520 --> 01:41:03,380
Calm yourself, Hagrid.

1499
01:41:05,360 --> 01:41:08,420
If the governors desire my removal...

1500
01:41:08,430 --> 01:41:09,950
...I will, of course,

1501
01:41:09,960 --> 01:41:11,520
step aside.

1502
01:41:13,670 --> 01:41:15,590
However...

1503
01:41:16,500 --> 01:41:21,230
...you will find that help will always be given at Hogwarts...

1504
01:41:21,240 --> 01:41:23,330
...to those who...

1505
01:41:23,340 --> 01:41:25,580
...ask for it.

1506
01:41:32,420 --> 01:41:34,580
Admirable sentiments.

1507
01:41:34,990 --> 01:41:36,480
Shall we?

1508
01:41:48,830 --> 01:41:50,230
Fudge.

1509
01:41:52,100 --> 01:41:53,630
Come, Hagrid.

1510
01:41:54,940 --> 01:41:56,430
Well?

1511
01:41:57,280 --> 01:41:58,830
If...

1512
01:41:58,840 --> 01:42:01,340
If anybody was looking for some stuff...

1513
01:42:01,510 --> 01:42:03,070
...then all they'd have to do would be

1514
01:42:03,080 --> 01:42:05,820
to follow the spiders.

1515
01:42:06,490 --> 01:42:07,280
Yep.

1516
01:42:07,290 --> 01:42:09,140
That would lead them right.

1517
01:42:09,350 --> 01:42:11,020
That's all I have to say.

1518
01:42:13,090 --> 01:42:16,090
Oh, and someone will need to feed Fang while I'm away.

1519
01:42:20,170 --> 01:42:21,590
Good boy.

1520
01:42:28,240 --> 01:42:29,800
Hagrid's right.

1521
01:42:30,410 --> 01:42:31,730
With Dumbledore gone,

1522
01:42:31,740 --> 01:42:33,510
there'll be an attack a day.

1523
01:42:33,780 --> 01:42:35,100
Look.

1524
01:42:41,490 --> 01:42:42,620
Come on.

1525
01:42:46,790 --> 01:42:48,080
Come on, Fang.

1526
01:43:07,380 --> 01:43:08,510
Come on.

1527
01:43:08,780 --> 01:43:10,070
What?

1528
01:43:10,380 --> 01:43:11,970
You heard what Hagrid said.

1529
01:43:11,980 --> 01:43:13,280
Follow the spiders.

1530
01:43:13,290 --> 01:43:15,580
They're heading to the Dark Forest.

1531
01:43:18,360 --> 01:43:19,950
Why spiders?

1532
01:43:19,960 --> 01:43:20,820
Why

1533
01:43:20,830 --> 01:43:22,960
couldn't it be "follow the butterflies"?

1534
01:43:58,700 --> 01:44:00,760
Harry, I don't like this.

1535
01:44:06,370 --> 01:44:08,570
Harry, I don't like this at all.

1536
01:44:21,250 --> 01:44:23,280
Can we go back now?

1537
01:44:23,790 --> 01:44:24,990
Come on.

1538
01:45:15,340 --> 01:45:17,940
Who is it?

1539
01:45:18,810 --> 01:45:20,340
Don't panic.

1540
01:45:20,350 --> 01:45:22,100
Hagrid?

1541
01:45:22,110 --> 01:45:24,140
Is that you?

1542
01:45:24,280 --> 01:45:26,280
We're friends of Hagrid's.

1543
01:45:44,300 --> 01:45:45,390
And you?

1544
01:45:45,400 --> 01:45:48,200
You're Aragog, aren't you?

1545
01:45:48,210 --> 01:45:49,530
Yes.

1546
01:45:49,540 --> 01:45:53,640
Hagrid has never sent men into our hollow before.

1547
01:45:53,650 --> 01:45:54,940
He's in trouble.

1548
01:45:54,950 --> 01:45:57,270
Up at the school, there have been attacks.

1549
01:45:57,280 --> 01:45:59,210
They think it's Hagrid.

1550
01:45:59,220 --> 01:46:03,110
They think he opened the Chamber of Secrets. Like before.

1551
01:46:03,120 --> 01:46:04,950
That's a lie.

1552
01:46:05,690 --> 01:46:09,450
Hagrid never opened the Chamber of Secrets.

1553
01:46:09,460 --> 01:46:11,250
Then you're not the monster?

1554
01:46:11,260 --> 01:46:12,550
No.

1555
01:46:12,560 --> 01:46:15,620
The monster was born in the castle.

1556
01:46:15,630 --> 01:46:19,290
I came to Hagrid from a distant land in the pocket

1557
01:46:19,300 --> 01:46:21,960
of a traveler.

1558
01:46:22,040 --> 01:46:23,860
-Harry.  -

1559
01:46:25,310 --> 01:46:27,500
But if you're not the monster,

1560
01:46:27,510 --> 01:46:29,870
then what did kill that girl 50 years ago?

1561
01:46:29,880 --> 01:46:33,280
We do not speak of it.

1562
01:46:33,320 --> 01:46:38,810
It is an ancient creature we spiders fear above all others.

1563
01:46:39,160 --> 01:46:41,390
But have you seen it?

1564
01:46:41,460 --> 01:46:44,050
but the box in which Hagrid kept me.

1565
01:46:44,060 --> 01:46:47,460
I never saw any part of the castle

1566
01:46:47,470 --> 01:46:49,220
The girl

1567
01:46:49,230 --> 01:46:50,830
was discovered in a bathroom.

1568
01:46:50,840 --> 01:46:52,890
When I was accused,

1569
01:46:52,900 --> 01:46:55,260
Hagrid brought me here.

1570
01:46:55,540 --> 01:46:57,870
-Harry!  -What?

1571
01:47:10,460 --> 01:47:11,650
Well,

1572
01:47:11,660 --> 01:47:13,220
thank you.

1573
01:47:14,430 --> 01:47:16,560
We'll just go.

1574
01:47:16,960 --> 01:47:18,630
Go?

1575
01:47:18,660 --> 01:47:20,820
I think not.

1576
01:47:20,830 --> 01:47:22,920
My sons and daughters

1577
01:47:22,930 --> 01:47:26,470
do not harm Hagrid on my command.

1578
01:47:26,570 --> 01:47:30,530
But I cannot deny them fresh meat...

1579
01:47:30,540 --> 01:47:33,040
...when it wanders so willingly into our midst.

1580
01:47:33,650 --> 01:47:37,810
Goodbye, friend of Hagrid.

1581
01:47:37,820 --> 01:47:39,950
Can we panic now?

1582
01:47:50,160 --> 01:47:51,930
Know any spells?

1583
01:47:52,200 --> 01:47:53,420
One,

1584
01:47:53,430 --> 01:47:55,490
but it's not powerful enough for all of them.

1585
01:47:55,500 --> 01:47:57,700
Where's Hermione when you need her?

1586
01:48:11,850 --> 01:48:13,120
Let's go!

1587
01:48:18,290 --> 01:48:20,150
Arania Exumai!

1588
01:48:25,860 --> 01:48:27,220
Go!

1589
01:48:44,950 --> 01:48:46,720
Glad we're out of there.

1590
01:48:53,790 --> 01:48:54,880
Arania

1591
01:48:54,890 --> 01:48:56,350
Exumai!

1592
01:49:01,930 --> 01:49:03,670
Thanks for that.

1593
01:49:03,700 --> 01:49:05,260
Don't mention it.

1594
01:49:16,680 --> 01:49:18,310
Get us out of here.

1595
01:49:19,320 --> 01:49:20,640
Now!

1596
01:49:23,120 --> 01:49:27,150
Come on! Come on, move faster!

1597
01:49:30,060 --> 01:49:32,090
Come on! Go!

1598
01:49:48,780 --> 01:49:50,410
Get us in the air.

1599
01:49:52,250 --> 01:49:54,280
The flying gear's jammed!

1600
01:49:57,660 --> 01:49:58,920
Come on! Pull!

1601
01:50:00,090 --> 01:50:01,620
I'm trying!

1602
01:50:30,660 --> 01:50:32,410
Follow the spiders.

1603
01:50:32,420 --> 01:50:33,850
Follow the spiders.

1604
01:50:33,860 --> 01:50:35,750
If Hagrid ever gets out of Azkaban,

1605
01:50:35,760 --> 01:50:37,120
I'll kill him.

1606
01:50:52,180 --> 01:50:55,440
I mean, what was the point of sending us in there?

1607
01:50:55,450 --> 01:50:57,110
What have we found out?

1608
01:50:57,720 --> 01:50:59,780
We know one thing.

1609
01:51:00,290 --> 01:51:03,250
Hagrid never opened the Chamber of Secrets.

1610
01:51:03,890 --> 01:51:05,850
He was innocent.

1611
01:51:21,510 --> 01:51:23,270
Wish you were here, Hermione.

1612
01:51:24,340 --> 01:51:25,870
We need you.

1613
01:51:27,610 --> 01:51:29,780
Now more than ever.

1614
01:51:46,530 --> 01:51:48,160
What's that?

1615
01:51:48,500 --> 01:51:49,990
Ron.

1616
01:51:50,840 --> 01:51:54,400
This is why Hermione was in the library the day she was attacked.

1617
01:51:56,040 --> 01:51:57,330
Come on.

1618
01:51:58,080 --> 01:52:01,140
Of the many fearsome beasts that roam our land...

1619
01:52:01,150 --> 01:52:03,270
...none is more deadly than the basilisk.

1620
01:52:03,280 --> 01:52:05,610
Capable of living for hundreds of years...

1621
01:52:05,620 --> 01:52:09,340
...instant death awaits any who meet this giant serpent's eye.

1622
01:52:09,350 --> 01:52:11,250
Spiders flee before it.

1623
01:52:11,260 --> 01:52:12,810
Ron, this is it.

1624
01:52:12,820 --> 01:52:15,550
The monster in the Chamber of Secrets is a basilisk.

1625
01:52:15,560 --> 01:52:17,620
That's why I can hear it speak.

1626
01:52:17,630 --> 01:52:19,520
It's a snake.

1627
01:52:19,730 --> 01:52:21,090
But if...

1628
01:52:21,100 --> 01:52:22,860
...it kills by looking people in the eye,

1629
01:52:22,870 --> 01:52:24,790
why is it no one's dead?

1630
01:52:35,980 --> 01:52:38,480
Because no one did look it in the eye.

1631
01:52:40,890 --> 01:52:43,020
Not directly, at least.

1632
01:52:44,690 --> 01:52:47,080
Colin saw it through his camera.

1633
01:52:47,090 --> 01:52:49,620
Justin...Justin must have seen the basilisk

1634
01:52:49,630 --> 01:52:51,190
through Nearly Headless Nick.

1635
01:52:51,200 --> 01:52:52,520
Nick got the full blast of it.

1636
01:52:52,530 --> 01:52:54,860
But he's a ghost, he couldn't die again.

1637
01:52:55,370 --> 01:52:57,460
And Hermione...

1638
01:52:57,540 --> 01:52:58,830
...had the mirror.

1639
01:52:58,840 --> 01:53:01,260
I bet you she was using it to look around corners

1640
01:53:01,270 --> 01:53:02,230
in case it came along.

1641
01:53:02,240 --> 01:53:03,700
And Mrs. Norris?

1642
01:53:03,710 --> 01:53:05,170
I'm pretty sure she didn't have a camera...

1643
01:53:05,180 --> 01:53:06,640
or a mirror, Harry.

1644
01:53:08,850 --> 01:53:13,240
The water. There was water on the floor that night.

1645
01:53:13,250 --> 01:53:16,650
She only saw the basilisk's reflection.

1646
01:53:22,760 --> 01:53:24,990
Spiders flee before it.

1647
01:53:25,000 --> 01:53:26,520
It all fits.

1648
01:53:26,530 --> 01:53:28,820
But how's a basilisk been getting around?

1649
01:53:28,830 --> 01:53:31,930
A dirty, great snake. Someone would have seen it.

1650
01:53:32,040 --> 01:53:34,130
Hermione's answered that too.

1651
01:53:34,140 --> 01:53:35,400
Pipes?

1652
01:53:35,410 --> 01:53:37,300
It's using the plumbing.

1653
01:53:37,710 --> 01:53:39,300
Remember what Aragog said

1654
01:53:39,310 --> 01:53:41,770
about that girl 50 years ago?

1655
01:53:42,010 --> 01:53:44,310
She died in a bathroom?

1656
01:53:44,320 --> 01:53:46,410
What if she never left?

1657
01:53:47,080 --> 01:53:48,940
Moaning Myrtle.

1658
01:53:49,350 --> 01:53:50,610
All students...

1659
01:53:50,620 --> 01:53:53,180
...are to return to their house dormitories at once.

1660
01:53:53,190 --> 01:53:56,820
All teachers to the second-floor corridor immediately.

1661
01:54:02,000 --> 01:54:03,620
As you can see,

1662
01:54:03,630 --> 01:54:05,630
the Heir of Slytherin

1663
01:54:05,640 --> 01:54:07,900
has left another message.

1664
01:54:08,110 --> 01:54:10,300
Our worst fear has been realized.

1665
01:54:10,310 --> 01:54:13,000
A student has been taken by the monster...

1666
01:54:13,010 --> 01:54:15,640
...into the Chamber itself.

1667
01:54:16,010 --> 01:54:18,210
The students must be sent home.

1668
01:54:18,220 --> 01:54:21,380
I'm afraid this is the end of Hogwarts.

1669
01:54:24,060 --> 01:54:25,310
So sorry. Dozed off.

1670
01:54:25,320 --> 01:54:26,410
What have I missed?

1671
01:54:26,420 --> 01:54:29,480
A girl has been snatched by the monster, Lockhart.

1672
01:54:29,490 --> 01:54:31,120
Your moment has come at last.

1673
01:54:31,130 --> 01:54:32,920
My moment?

1674
01:54:32,930 --> 01:54:34,220
Weren't you saying just last night...

1675
01:54:34,230 --> 01:54:35,660
...that you've known all along...

1676
01:54:35,670 --> 01:54:38,330
...where the entrance to the Chamber of Secrets is?

1677
01:54:40,270 --> 01:54:42,060
That's settled.

1678
01:54:42,070 --> 01:54:45,710
We'll leave you to deal with the monster, Gilderoy.

1679
01:54:45,810 --> 01:54:49,170
Your skills, after all, are legend.

1680
01:54:49,550 --> 01:54:51,170
Very well.

1681
01:54:51,180 --> 01:54:55,210
I'll just be in my office getting...

1682
01:54:55,220 --> 01:54:56,950
Getting ready.

1683
01:55:00,120 --> 01:55:03,190
Who is it that the monster's taken, Minerva?

1684
01:55:03,430 --> 01:55:05,420
Ginny Weasley.

1685
01:55:16,670 --> 01:55:20,270
Her skeleton will lie in the Chamber forever

1686
01:55:23,850 --> 01:55:25,480
Ginny.

1687
01:55:27,720 --> 01:55:29,180
Lockhart may be useless,

1688
01:55:29,190 --> 01:55:31,410
but he's going to try and get into the Chamber.

1689
01:55:31,420 --> 01:55:34,250
At least we can tell him what we know.

1690
01:55:35,490 --> 01:55:37,990
Professor, we have some information for you.

1691
01:55:39,730 --> 01:55:41,360
Are you going somewhere?

1692
01:55:41,370 --> 01:55:42,590
Well, yes.

1693
01:55:42,600 --> 01:55:43,820
Urgent call.

1694
01:55:43,830 --> 01:55:45,190
Unavoidable. Got to go.

1695
01:55:45,200 --> 01:55:46,530
What about my sister?

1696
01:55:46,540 --> 01:55:50,460
Well...As to that, most unfortunate.

1697
01:55:50,470 --> 01:55:52,400
No one regrets more than I.

1698
01:55:52,410 --> 01:55:55,040
You're the Defense Against the Dark Arts teacher.

1699
01:55:55,050 --> 01:55:56,400
You can't go now.

1700
01:55:56,410 --> 01:55:58,110
I must say, when I took the job,

1701
01:55:58,120 --> 01:55:59,640
there was nothing in the description...

1702
01:55:59,650 --> 01:56:01,180
You're running away?

1703
01:56:01,190 --> 01:56:02,910
After all you did in your books?

1704
01:56:02,920 --> 01:56:04,010
Books can be misleading.

1705
01:56:04,020 --> 01:56:05,310
You wrote them.

1706
01:56:05,320 --> 01:56:06,850
My dear boy, do use your common sense.

1707
01:56:06,860 --> 01:56:08,680
My books wouldn't have sold half as well

1708
01:56:08,690 --> 01:56:11,390
if people didn't think I'd done those things.

1709
01:56:11,830 --> 01:56:13,450
You're a fraud.

1710
01:56:13,460 --> 01:56:16,560
You've been taking credit for what other wizards have done.

1711
01:56:16,570 --> 01:56:18,530
Is there anything you can do?

1712
01:56:18,540 --> 01:56:19,460
Yes,

1713
01:56:19,470 --> 01:56:21,060
now you mention it.

1714
01:56:21,070 --> 01:56:23,500
I'm rather gifted with Memory Charms.

1715
01:56:23,510 --> 01:56:24,530
Otherwise, all those wizards

1716
01:56:24,540 --> 01:56:26,300
would have gone blabbing.

1717
01:56:26,310 --> 01:56:28,370
I'd never have sold another book.

1718
01:56:28,910 --> 01:56:30,670
In fact,

1719
01:56:30,680 --> 01:56:35,010
I'm going to have to do the same to you.

1720
01:56:35,790 --> 01:56:38,050
Don't even think about it.

1721
01:56:49,370 --> 01:56:51,190
Who's there?

1722
01:56:53,200 --> 01:56:54,800
Hello, Harry.

1723
01:56:56,170 --> 01:56:57,770
What do you want?

1724
01:56:57,980 --> 01:57:01,900
To ask you how you died.

1725
01:57:03,710 --> 01:57:06,310
It was dreadful.

1726
01:57:06,320 --> 01:57:10,210
It happened right here in this very cubicle.

1727
01:57:10,220 --> 01:57:14,450
I'd hidden because Olive Hornby was teasing me about my glasses.

1728
01:57:14,460 --> 01:57:15,850
I was crying,

1729
01:57:15,860 --> 01:57:19,420
and then I heard somebody come in.

1730
01:57:19,430 --> 01:57:20,820
Who was it, Myrtle?

1731
01:57:20,830 --> 01:57:23,120
I don't know.

1732
01:57:23,130 --> 01:57:26,100
I was distraught!

1733
01:57:27,040 --> 01:57:28,860
But they said something funny,

1734
01:57:28,870 --> 01:57:30,730
a kind of made-up language.

1735
01:57:30,740 --> 01:57:32,700
And I realized it was a boy,

1736
01:57:32,710 --> 01:57:34,040
so I unlocked the door...

1737
01:57:34,050 --> 01:57:36,000
to tell him to go away...

1738
01:57:36,010 --> 01:57:40,170
...and I died.

1739
01:57:40,280 --> 01:57:42,110
Just like that?

1740
01:57:42,120 --> 01:57:43,180
How?

1741
01:57:43,190 --> 01:57:47,880
I just remember seeing a pair of great, big, yellow eyes...

1742
01:57:47,890 --> 01:57:51,250
...over there by that sink.

1743
01:58:16,850 --> 01:58:18,420
This is it.

1744
01:58:19,790 --> 01:58:21,220
This is it, Ron.

1745
01:58:21,790 --> 01:58:24,890
I think this is the entrance to the Chamber of Secrets.

1746
01:58:26,730 --> 01:58:28,360
Say something.

1747
01:58:28,530 --> 01:58:30,820
Harry, say something in Parseltongue.

1748
01:59:22,920 --> 01:59:23,880
Excellent, Harry.

1749
01:59:23,890 --> 01:59:25,250
Good work.

1750
01:59:25,260 --> 01:59:27,450
Well, then, I'll just be...

1751
01:59:27,460 --> 01:59:28,750
There's no need for me to stay.

1752
01:59:29,660 --> 01:59:32,090
Yes, there is.

1753
01:59:33,900 --> 01:59:35,190
You first.

1754
01:59:35,200 --> 01:59:36,890
Now, boys, what good will it do?

1755
01:59:36,900 --> 01:59:38,490
Better you than us.

1756
01:59:38,500 --> 01:59:42,100
But...Obviously, yes.

1757
01:59:46,910 --> 01:59:48,870
Sure you don't want to test it first?

1758
01:59:56,350 --> 01:59:59,140
It's really quite filthy down here.

1759
02:00:00,090 --> 02:00:01,580
All right.

1760
02:00:01,760 --> 02:00:03,080
Let's go.

1761
02:00:03,230 --> 02:00:04,820
Oh, Harry?

1762
02:00:05,030 --> 02:00:06,550
If you die down there,

1763
02:00:06,560 --> 02:00:09,360
you're welcome to share my toilet.

1764
02:00:12,500 --> 02:00:14,130
Thanks, Myrtle.

1765
02:00:43,570 --> 02:00:44,630
Now, remember,

1766
02:00:44,640 --> 02:00:46,060
Any sign of movement,

1767
02:00:46,070 --> 02:00:48,240
close your eyes straightaway.

1768
02:00:49,710 --> 02:00:51,030
Go on.

1769
02:00:55,110 --> 02:00:56,400
This way.

1770
02:01:03,490 --> 02:01:05,250
What's this?

1771
02:01:05,260 --> 02:01:07,080
It looks like...

1772
02:01:07,420 --> 02:01:08,980
...a snake.

1773
02:01:08,990 --> 02:01:10,620
It's a snakeskin.

1774
02:01:10,630 --> 02:01:12,290
Bloody hell.

1775
02:01:12,700 --> 02:01:15,860
Whatever shed this must be 60 feet long.

1776
02:01:16,270 --> 02:01:18,000
Or more.

1777
02:01:20,440 --> 02:01:22,970
Heart of a lion, this one.

1778
02:01:27,040 --> 02:01:30,540
The adventure ends here, boys.

1779
02:01:30,550 --> 02:01:33,640
But don't fret. The world...

1780
02:01:33,650 --> 02:01:36,110
...will know our story.

1781
02:01:36,120 --> 02:01:39,510
How I was too late to save the girl.

1782
02:01:39,520 --> 02:01:41,280
How you two...

1783
02:01:41,290 --> 02:01:45,930
tragically lost your minds at the sight of her mangled body.

1784
02:01:46,930 --> 02:01:48,430
So...

1785
02:01:49,570 --> 02:01:51,930
you first, Mr. Potter.

1786
02:01:52,140 --> 02:01:55,900
Say goodbye to your memories.

1787
02:01:57,410 --> 02:01:59,540
Obliviate!

1788
02:02:25,940 --> 02:02:27,400
Harry.

1789
02:02:28,940 --> 02:02:30,260
Harry.

1790
02:02:33,280 --> 02:02:34,230
Ron.

1791
02:02:34,240 --> 02:02:35,470
Ron, are you okay?

1792
02:02:35,480 --> 02:02:36,940
I'm fine.

1793
02:02:40,080 --> 02:02:41,650
Hello.

1794
02:02:42,550 --> 02:02:44,010
Who are you?

1795
02:02:45,820 --> 02:02:47,110
Ron Weasley.

1796
02:02:47,120 --> 02:02:48,450
Really?

1797
02:02:48,590 --> 02:02:51,620
And who am I?

1798
02:02:53,200 --> 02:02:55,620
Lockhart's Memory Charm backfired.

1799
02:02:55,630 --> 02:02:57,660
He hasn't got a clue who he is.

1800
02:02:57,670 --> 02:03:01,730
It's an odd sort of place, isn't it?

1801
02:03:02,510 --> 02:03:04,000
Do you live here?

1802
02:03:05,340 --> 02:03:06,670
No.

1803
02:03:06,680 --> 02:03:08,000
Really?

1804
02:03:12,450 --> 02:03:13,810
What do I do now?

1805
02:03:13,820 --> 02:03:16,280
you wait here and try and shift some of this rock...

1806
02:03:16,290 --> 02:03:17,610
...so we can get back through.

1807
02:03:17,620 --> 02:03:19,410
I'll go on and find Ginny.

1808
02:03:19,420 --> 02:03:20,780
Okay.

1809
02:04:45,040 --> 02:04:46,370
Ginny!

1810
02:04:54,420 --> 02:04:56,610
Ginny, please don't be dead.

1811
02:04:56,620 --> 02:05:00,550
Wake up, wake up. Please wake up.

1812
02:05:01,260 --> 02:05:02,920
She won't wake.

1813
02:05:08,770 --> 02:05:09,990
Tom.

1814
02:05:10,000 --> 02:05:11,290
Tom Riddle.

1815
02:05:11,300 --> 02:05:13,160
What do you mean, she won't wake?

1816
02:05:13,170 --> 02:05:15,360
She's not...? She's still alive,

1817
02:05:15,370 --> 02:05:17,070
but only just.

1818
02:05:17,670 --> 02:05:18,970
Are you a ghost?

1819
02:05:18,980 --> 02:05:20,200
A memory...

1820
02:05:20,210 --> 02:05:22,810
...preserved in a diary for 50 years.

1821
02:05:25,220 --> 02:05:27,110
She's cold as ice.

1822
02:05:27,120 --> 02:05:29,110
Ginny, please don't be dead.

1823
02:05:29,120 --> 02:05:30,610
Wake up.

1824
02:05:30,620 --> 02:05:31,810
You've got to help me, Tom.

1825
02:05:31,820 --> 02:05:33,050
There's a basilisk.

1826
02:05:33,060 --> 02:05:35,120
It won't come until it's called.

1827
02:05:38,600 --> 02:05:40,120
Give me my wand, Tom.

1828
02:05:40,130 --> 02:05:41,830
You won't be needing it.

1829
02:05:42,430 --> 02:05:44,320
We've got to go. We've got to save her.

1830
02:05:44,330 --> 02:05:45,730
I'm afraid I can't do that.

1831
02:05:45,740 --> 02:05:48,800
You see, as poor Ginny grows weaker,

1832
02:05:48,810 --> 02:05:50,440
I grow stronger.

1833
02:05:51,340 --> 02:05:52,570
Yes, Harry,

1834
02:05:52,580 --> 02:05:53,730
it was Ginny Weasley...

1835
02:05:53,740 --> 02:05:55,940
...who opened the Chamber of Secrets.

1836
02:05:56,050 --> 02:05:58,710
No. She couldn't. She wouldn't.

1837
02:05:58,720 --> 02:06:01,880
It was Ginny who set the basilisk on the Mudbloods and Filch's cat...

1838
02:06:01,890 --> 02:06:04,480
...Ginny who wrote the threatening messages on the walls.

1839
02:06:04,490 --> 02:06:05,580
But why?

1840
02:06:05,590 --> 02:06:07,550
Because I told her to.

1841
02:06:08,030 --> 02:06:11,620
You'll find I can be very persuasive.

1842
02:06:11,630 --> 02:06:13,090
Not that she knew what she was doing.

1843
02:06:13,100 --> 02:06:15,860
She was, shall we say, in a kind of trance.

1844
02:06:17,000 --> 02:06:19,630
Still, the power of the diary began to scare her.

1845
02:06:19,640 --> 02:06:22,260
She tried to dispose of it in the girls' bathroom.

1846
02:06:22,270 --> 02:06:23,900
And then...

1847
02:06:23,910 --> 02:06:25,130
who should find it?

1848
02:06:25,140 --> 02:06:26,600
But you...

1849
02:06:26,810 --> 02:06:30,500
...the very person I was most anxious to meet.

1850
02:06:30,510 --> 02:06:32,980
And why did you want to meet me?

1851
02:06:33,020 --> 02:06:34,640
I knew I had to talk to you,

1852
02:06:34,650 --> 02:06:36,440
meet you if I could.

1853
02:06:36,450 --> 02:06:37,130
So I decided

1854
02:06:37,140 --> 02:06:39,750
to show you my capture of that brainless oaf Hagrid...

1855
02:06:39,760 --> 02:06:40,750
...to gain your trust.

1856
02:06:40,760 --> 02:06:42,790
Hagrid's my friend.

1857
02:06:44,030 --> 02:06:46,090
And you framed him, didn't you?

1858
02:06:46,100 --> 02:06:48,690
It was my word against Hagrid's.

1859
02:06:48,700 --> 02:06:49,790
Only Dumbledore...

1860
02:06:49,800 --> 02:06:51,760
...seemed to think he was innocent.

1861
02:06:52,300 --> 02:06:54,490
I'll bet Dumbledore saw right through you.

1862
02:06:54,500 --> 02:06:58,330
He certainly kept an annoyingly close watch on me after that.

1863
02:06:58,380 --> 02:07:00,450
I knew it wouldn't be safe to open the Chamber again

1864
02:07:00,460 --> 02:07:01,470
while I was still at school...

1865
02:07:01,480 --> 02:07:03,570
...so I decided to leave behind a diary...

1866
02:07:03,580 --> 02:07:05,910
...preserving my 1 6-year-old self in its pages...

1867
02:07:05,920 --> 02:07:07,040
...so that one day...

1868
02:07:07,050 --> 02:07:08,840
...I would be able to lead another...

1869
02:07:08,850 --> 02:07:11,780
...to finish Salazar Slytherin's noble work.

1870
02:07:11,790 --> 02:07:14,180
Well, you haven't finished it this time.

1871
02:07:14,190 --> 02:07:15,250
In a few hours,

1872
02:07:15,260 --> 02:07:17,280
the Mandrake Draught will be ready.

1873
02:07:17,290 --> 02:07:18,790
And everyone who was Petrified

1874
02:07:18,800 --> 02:07:20,550
will be all right again.

1875
02:07:20,560 --> 02:07:22,060
Haven't I told you?

1876
02:07:22,070 --> 02:07:25,190
Killing Mudbloods doesn't matter to me anymore.

1877
02:07:25,940 --> 02:07:31,030
For many months now, my new target has been you.

1878
02:07:33,080 --> 02:07:35,800
How is it that a baby with no extraordinary magical talent...

1879
02:07:35,810 --> 02:07:37,140
...was able to defeat...

1880
02:07:37,150 --> 02:07:38,870
...the greatest wizard of all time?

1881
02:07:38,880 --> 02:07:42,100
How did you escape with nothing but a scar...

1882
02:07:42,110 --> 02:07:44,540
...while Lord Voldemort's powers were destroyed?

1883
02:07:44,550 --> 02:07:46,350
Why do you care how I escaped?

1884
02:07:46,360 --> 02:07:48,950
Voldemort was after your time.

1885
02:07:48,960 --> 02:07:50,120
Voldemort...

1886
02:07:50,130 --> 02:07:52,550
...is my past,

1887
02:07:52,560 --> 02:07:55,560
present and future.

1888
02:08:17,490 --> 02:08:19,720
You...you're the Heir of Slytherin.

1889
02:08:22,490 --> 02:08:24,020
You're Voldemort.

1890
02:08:24,030 --> 02:08:26,220
Surely you didn't think...

1891
02:08:26,230 --> 02:08:27,550
...I was going to keep...

1892
02:08:27,560 --> 02:08:30,360
my filthy Muggle father's name?

1893
02:08:30,970 --> 02:08:31,930
No.

1894
02:08:31,940 --> 02:08:33,690
I fashioned myself a new name,

1895
02:08:33,700 --> 02:08:36,030
a name I knew wizards everywhere would one day fear to speak...

1896
02:08:36,040 --> 02:08:39,670
...when I became the greatest sorcerer in the world.

1897
02:08:39,680 --> 02:08:40,930
Albus Dumbledore...

1898
02:08:40,940 --> 02:08:42,870
...is the greatest sorcerer in the world.

1899
02:08:42,880 --> 02:08:44,540
Dumbledore's been driven out of

1900
02:08:44,550 --> 02:08:46,410
this castle by the mere memory of me.

1901
02:08:46,420 --> 02:08:47,710
He'll never be gone.

1902
02:08:47,720 --> 02:08:50,920
Not as long as those who remain are loyal to him.

1903
02:08:58,100 --> 02:08:59,950
Fawkes?

1904
02:09:15,380 --> 02:09:16,640
So this is what Dumbledore...

1905
02:09:16,650 --> 02:09:19,010
...sends his great defender.

1906
02:09:19,020 --> 02:09:20,410
A songbird...

1907
02:09:20,420 --> 02:09:22,450
...and an old hat.

1908
02:09:36,000 --> 02:09:38,790
Let's match the power of Lord Voldemort,

1909
02:09:38,800 --> 02:09:42,160
Heir of Salazar Slytherinagainst the famous...

1910
02:09:42,170 --> 02:09:44,200
...Harry Potter.

1911
02:09:58,090 --> 02:10:00,050
Parseltongue won't save you now, Potter.

1912
02:10:00,060 --> 02:10:01,880
It only obeys me.

1913
02:10:32,690 --> 02:10:34,080
No!

1914
02:10:34,660 --> 02:10:36,850
your bird may have blinded the basilisk,

1915
02:10:36,860 --> 02:10:39,460
but it can still hear you.

1916
02:12:21,260 --> 02:12:22,560
Yes, Potter.

1917
02:12:22,570 --> 02:12:24,420
The process is nearly complete.

1918
02:12:24,430 --> 02:12:26,960
In a few minutes, Ginny Weasley will be dead,

1919
02:12:26,970 --> 02:12:29,430
and I will cease to be a memory.

1920
02:12:29,610 --> 02:12:32,070
Lord Voldemort will return...

1921
02:12:32,780 --> 02:12:37,540
...very much alive.

1922
02:12:37,680 --> 02:12:39,240
Ginny?

1923
02:14:55,420 --> 02:14:57,110
Remarkable, isn't it...

1924
02:14:57,120 --> 02:15:00,760
...how quickly the venom of the basilisk penetrates the body?

1925
02:15:01,190 --> 02:15:04,280
I'd guess you have little more than a minute to live.

1926
02:15:04,290 --> 02:15:07,790
You'll be with your dear Mudblood mother soon, Harry.

1927
02:15:13,340 --> 02:15:14,490
Funny,

1928
02:15:14,500 --> 02:15:17,030
the damage a silly little book can do...

1929
02:15:17,040 --> 02:15:18,200
...especially...

1930
02:15:18,210 --> 02:15:21,940
...in the hands of a silly little girl.

1931
02:15:25,180 --> 02:15:26,810
What are you doing?

1932
02:15:29,620 --> 02:15:31,890
Stop. No!

1933
02:16:24,540 --> 02:16:26,140
Ginny.

1934
02:16:28,210 --> 02:16:29,640
Harry.

1935
02:16:30,210 --> 02:16:31,540
It was me.

1936
02:16:31,550 --> 02:16:32,570
But I swear,

1937
02:16:32,580 --> 02:16:34,240
I didn't mean to.

1938
02:16:34,250 --> 02:16:36,280
Riddle made me,

1939
02:16:36,350 --> 02:16:37,880
and...

1940
02:16:38,450 --> 02:16:41,310
Harry, you're hurt.

1941
02:16:41,320 --> 02:16:42,820
Don't worry.

1942
02:16:42,830 --> 02:16:44,220
Ginny,

1943
02:16:44,230 --> 02:16:46,590
you need to get yourself out.

1944
02:16:46,600 --> 02:16:47,820
Follow the Chamber

1945
02:16:47,830 --> 02:16:49,960
and you'll find Ron.

1946
02:17:02,210 --> 02:17:05,000
You were brilliant, Fawkes.

1947
02:17:05,420 --> 02:17:07,810
I just wasn't quick enough.

1948
02:17:28,640 --> 02:17:30,370
Of course.

1949
02:17:30,710 --> 02:17:33,310
Phoenix tears have healing powers.

1950
02:17:35,280 --> 02:17:36,740
Thanks.

1951
02:17:38,750 --> 02:17:40,520
It's all right, Ginny.

1952
02:17:41,920 --> 02:17:43,580
It's over.

1953
02:17:45,150 --> 02:17:47,010
It's just a memory.

1954
02:17:50,460 --> 02:17:52,350
Amazing!

1955
02:17:52,360 --> 02:17:55,890
This is just like magic!

1956
02:18:07,180 --> 02:18:10,000
You both realize, of course...

1957
02:18:10,010 --> 02:18:11,740
...that in the past few hours,

1958
02:18:11,750 --> 02:18:16,310
you have broken perhaps a dozen school rules.

1959
02:18:16,320 --> 02:18:17,280
Yes, sir.

1960
02:18:17,290 --> 02:18:20,390
There is sufficient evidence to have you both expelled.

1961
02:18:20,620 --> 02:18:22,120
Yes, sir.

1962
02:18:22,130 --> 02:18:23,720
Yes, sir.

1963
02:18:23,730 --> 02:18:26,290
Therefore, it is only fitting...

1964
02:18:26,460 --> 02:18:29,320
...that you both receive...

1965
02:18:29,330 --> 02:18:33,260
...Special Awards for Services to the School.

1966
02:18:35,670 --> 02:18:37,230
Thanks, sir.

1967
02:18:37,870 --> 02:18:39,130
Now, Mr. Weasley,

1968
02:18:39,140 --> 02:18:41,170
if you would have an owl...

1969
02:18:41,180 --> 02:18:43,910
...deliver these release papers to Azkaban.

1970
02:18:45,580 --> 02:18:47,210
I believe...

1971
02:18:47,220 --> 02:18:50,140
...we want our gamekeeper back.

1972
02:18:53,090 --> 02:18:54,620
Harry.

1973
02:18:55,260 --> 02:18:56,980
First,

1974
02:18:56,990 --> 02:18:59,490
I want to thank you, Harry.

1975
02:19:00,300 --> 02:19:04,000
You must have shown me real loyalty down in the Chamber.

1976
02:19:04,530 --> 02:19:09,260
Nothing but that could have called Fawkes to you.

1977
02:19:11,740 --> 02:19:13,600
And...

1978
02:19:13,810 --> 02:19:15,300
...second...

1979
02:19:15,310 --> 02:19:17,200
...I sense that...

1980
02:19:17,210 --> 02:19:19,610
...something is troubling you.

1981
02:19:20,320 --> 02:19:22,310
Am I right, Harry?

1982
02:19:24,790 --> 02:19:26,350
It's just...

1983
02:19:27,660 --> 02:19:28,650
you see, sir,

1984
02:19:28,660 --> 02:19:33,730
I couldn't help but notice certain things, certain..

1985
02:19:36,430 --> 02:19:38,700
Certain similarities between Tom Riddle and me.

1986
02:19:38,800 --> 02:19:40,060
I see.

1987
02:19:40,070 --> 02:19:41,530
Well,

1988
02:19:41,540 --> 02:19:45,330
you can speak Parseltongue, Harry. Why?

1989
02:19:46,310 --> 02:19:47,600
Because...

1990
02:19:47,610 --> 02:19:49,270
...Lord Voldemort...

1991
02:19:49,280 --> 02:19:52,270
can speak Parseltongue.

1992
02:19:53,080 --> 02:19:56,210
If I'm not mistaken, Harry...

1993
02:19:56,220 --> 02:20:00,110
...he transferred some of his powers to you...

1994
02:20:00,120 --> 02:20:02,790
...the night he gave you that scar.

1995
02:20:03,160 --> 02:20:07,730
Voldemort transferred some of his powers to me?

1996
02:20:09,130 --> 02:20:11,160
Not intentionally...

1997
02:20:12,770 --> 02:20:14,370
...but yes.

1998
02:20:16,510 --> 02:20:18,330
So the Sorting Hat was right.

1999
02:20:18,340 --> 02:20:19,900
I should be in Slytherin.

2000
02:20:19,910 --> 02:20:21,100
It's true, Harry.

2001
02:20:21,110 --> 02:20:25,270
You possess many of the qualities that Voldemort himself prizes.

2002
02:20:25,280 --> 02:20:26,340
Determination,

2003
02:20:26,350 --> 02:20:27,870
resourcefulness...

2004
02:20:27,880 --> 02:20:31,750
...and if I may say so, a certain disregard for the rules.

2005
02:20:32,690 --> 02:20:33,780
Why, then,

2006
02:20:33,790 --> 02:20:36,120
did the Sorting Hat place you in Gryffindor?

2007
02:20:37,590 --> 02:20:38,950
Because I asked it to.

2008
02:20:38,960 --> 02:20:41,420
Exactly, Harry. Exactly.

2009
02:20:41,430 --> 02:20:43,590
Which makes you different from Voldemort.

2010
02:20:43,600 --> 02:20:47,890
It is not our abilities that show what we truly are.

2011
02:20:47,900 --> 02:20:50,470
It is our choices.

2012
02:20:53,680 --> 02:20:54,800
If you want proof...

2013
02:20:54,810 --> 02:20:57,100
why you belong in Gryffindor...

2014
02:20:57,110 --> 02:20:58,500
...then I suggest you...

2015
02:20:58,510 --> 02:21:01,810
...look more closely at this.

2016
02:21:03,350 --> 02:21:04,740
Be careful.

2017
02:21:10,490 --> 02:21:12,190
Godric Gryffindor.

2018
02:21:13,200 --> 02:21:15,560
It would take a true Gryffindor...

2019
02:21:15,570 --> 02:21:17,730
...to pull that out of the hat.

2020
02:21:26,140 --> 02:21:27,770
Dobby.

2021
02:21:28,880 --> 02:21:31,170
So this is your master.

2022
02:21:31,180 --> 02:21:34,450
The family you serve is the Malfoys.

2023
02:21:35,550 --> 02:21:38,220
I'll deal with you later.

2024
02:21:44,630 --> 02:21:46,390
Out of my way, Potter.

2025
02:21:46,400 --> 02:21:47,720
So it's true.

2026
02:21:47,730 --> 02:21:50,160
You have returned.

2027
02:21:50,770 --> 02:21:52,260
When the governors learned...

2028
02:21:52,270 --> 02:21:55,060
that Arthur Weasley's daughter was taken into the Chamber,

2029
02:21:55,070 --> 02:21:56,830
they saw...

2030
02:21:56,840 --> 02:21:58,760
...fit to summon me back.

2031
02:21:58,770 --> 02:22:00,030
Ridiculous.

2032
02:22:00,040 --> 02:22:01,130
Curiously,

2033
02:22:01,140 --> 02:22:02,070
Lucius,

2034
02:22:02,080 --> 02:22:03,240
several of them...

2035
02:22:03,250 --> 02:22:06,570
...were under the impression that you would curse their family...

2036
02:22:06,580 --> 02:22:10,080
...if they did not agree to suspend me in the first place.

2037
02:22:10,090 --> 02:22:12,210
How dare you!

2038
02:22:12,220 --> 02:22:13,810
Beg your pardon?

2039
02:22:13,820 --> 02:22:17,750
My sole concern has always been and will always be...

2040
02:22:17,760 --> 02:22:20,550
...the welfare of this school...

2041
02:22:20,560 --> 02:22:22,460
...and, of course,

2042
02:22:22,470 --> 02:22:24,820
its students.

2043
02:22:28,840 --> 02:22:32,170
The culprit has been identified,

2044
02:22:32,180 --> 02:22:33,500
I presume?

2045
02:22:33,510 --> 02:22:35,140
Yes.

2046
02:22:36,580 --> 02:22:38,850
And?

2047
02:22:39,580 --> 02:22:41,410
Who was it?

2048
02:22:48,120 --> 02:22:49,860
Voldemort.

2049
02:22:51,960 --> 02:22:53,420
Only this time...

2050
02:22:53,430 --> 02:22:57,660
...he chose to act through somebody else...

2051
02:22:57,930 --> 02:23:01,760
...by means of this.

2052
02:23:04,170 --> 02:23:06,130
I...I see.

2053
02:23:07,280 --> 02:23:08,940
Fortunately,

2054
02:23:08,950 --> 02:23:11,770
our young Mr. Potter discovered it.

2055
02:23:11,780 --> 02:23:15,470
One hopes that no more of Lord Voldemort's old school-things...

2056
02:23:15,480 --> 02:23:21,900
...should find their way into innocent hands.

2057
02:23:21,910 --> 02:23:25,420
The consequences for the one responsible would be severe.

2058
02:23:26,660 --> 02:23:27,820
Well,

2059
02:23:27,830 --> 02:23:29,820
let us hope...

2060
02:23:29,830 --> 02:23:35,700
...that Mr. Potter will always be around to save the day.

2061
02:23:36,010 --> 02:23:37,530
Don't worry.

2062
02:23:37,770 --> 02:23:39,440
I will be.

2063
02:23:48,480 --> 02:23:50,150
Dumbledore.

2064
02:23:51,690 --> 02:23:53,310
Come, Dobby.

2065
02:23:53,320 --> 02:23:55,090
We're leaving.

2066
02:24:12,440 --> 02:24:14,040
Sir?

2067
02:24:14,410 --> 02:24:16,770
I wonder if I could have that?

2068
02:24:23,320 --> 02:24:25,090
Mr. Malfoy.

2069
02:24:25,120 --> 02:24:26,820
Mr. Malfoy.

2070
02:24:27,790 --> 02:24:29,680
I have something of yours.

2071
02:24:31,630 --> 02:24:33,090
Mine?

2072
02:24:33,100 --> 02:24:34,750
I don't know what you're talking about.

2073
02:24:34,760 --> 02:24:36,490
I think you do, sir.

2074
02:24:36,500 --> 02:24:37,720
I think you slipped the diary

2075
02:24:37,730 --> 02:24:41,830
into Ginny Weasley's cauldron that day at Diagon Alley.

2076
02:24:41,840 --> 02:24:44,160
you do, do you?

2077
02:24:51,410 --> 02:24:55,450
Why don't you prove it?

2078
02:25:00,990 --> 02:25:02,480
Come, Dobby.

2079
02:25:04,630 --> 02:25:06,190
Open it.

2080
02:25:10,030 --> 02:25:11,660
Dobby.

2081
02:25:11,700 --> 02:25:15,130
Master has given Dobby a sock.

2082
02:25:15,140 --> 02:25:17,300
What? I didn't give...

2083
02:25:17,440 --> 02:25:21,370
Master has presented Dobby with clothes.

2084
02:25:21,380 --> 02:25:24,910
Dobby is free.

2085
02:25:30,950 --> 02:25:34,810
You lost me my servant!

2086
02:25:41,700 --> 02:25:45,520
You shall not harm Harry Potter.

2087
02:25:57,810 --> 02:26:01,670
Your parents were meddlesome fools too.

2088
02:26:01,680 --> 02:26:03,510
Mark my words, Potter.

2089
02:26:03,520 --> 02:26:05,080
One day soon...

2090
02:26:05,090 --> 02:26:10,480
...you are going to meet the same sticky end.

2091
02:26:16,000 --> 02:26:18,790
Harry Potter freed Dobby.

2092
02:26:18,800 --> 02:26:21,800
How can Dobby ever repay him?

2093
02:26:22,240 --> 02:26:24,330
Just promise me something.

2094
02:26:24,340 --> 02:26:26,540
Anything, sir.

2095
02:26:28,480 --> 02:26:31,210
Never try to save my life again.

2096
02:26:37,120 --> 02:26:38,610
Welcome back, Sir Nicholas.

2097
02:26:38,620 --> 02:26:39,980
Thank you.

2098
02:26:40,420 --> 02:26:41,810
Good evening, Sir Nicholas.

2099
02:26:41,820 --> 02:26:42,780
Good evening.

2100
02:26:42,790 --> 02:26:44,180
Good to see you, Sir Nicholas.

2101
02:26:44,190 --> 02:26:45,720
Thank you.

2102
02:26:47,230 --> 02:26:49,190
Hello.

2103
02:26:51,130 --> 02:26:52,290
Hermione!

2104
02:26:52,300 --> 02:26:54,090
Welcome back.

2105
02:26:54,100 --> 02:26:55,630
Thanks, Sir Nicholas.

2106
02:26:59,070 --> 02:27:00,270
Harry.

2107
02:27:00,280 --> 02:27:01,800
It's Hermione.

2108
02:27:28,370 --> 02:27:30,700
Welcome back, Hermione.

2109
02:27:30,840 --> 02:27:32,540
It's good to be back.

2110
02:27:33,080 --> 02:27:35,600
Congratulations. I can't believe you solved it.

2111
02:27:35,610 --> 02:27:38,200
We had loads of help from you.

2112
02:27:38,210 --> 02:27:40,180
We couldn't have done it without you.

2113
02:27:40,320 --> 02:27:41,670
Thanks.

2114
02:27:43,320 --> 02:27:46,210
Could I have your attention, please?

2115
02:27:50,330 --> 02:27:53,090
Before we begin the feast...

2116
02:27:53,100 --> 02:27:56,620
...Let us have a round of applause...

2117
02:27:56,630 --> 02:27:57,960
...for Professor Sprout,

2118
02:27:57,970 --> 02:27:59,590
Madam Pomfrey...

2119
02:27:59,600 --> 02:28:02,030
...whose Mandrake juice

2120
02:28:02,040 --> 02:28:07,210
...has been so successfully administered to all who had been Petrified.

2121
02:28:17,090 --> 02:28:22,450
Also, in light of the recent events as...

2122
02:28:22,460 --> 02:28:26,920
...a school treat all exams have been canceled.

2123
02:28:29,160 --> 02:28:30,830
Oh no.

2124
02:28:47,680 --> 02:28:49,250
Sorry I'm late.

2125
02:29:00,430 --> 02:29:03,460
Some ruddy bird called Errol.

2126
02:29:19,580 --> 02:29:21,840
And I'd just like to say...

2127
02:29:21,850 --> 02:29:25,510
...that if it hadn't been for you, Harry and Ron...

2128
02:29:25,520 --> 02:29:28,350
...and Hermione, of course.

2129
02:29:29,390 --> 02:29:33,620
I would still be you-know-where...

2130
02:29:33,630 --> 02:29:37,760
...so I'd just like to say thanks.

2131
02:29:46,480 --> 02:29:49,300
There's no Hogwarts without you, Hagrid.

